<node id="Calcium Ions">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium ions are chemical species released from phosphogypsum that participate in alkaline precipitation reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Positively charged ions released into solution during the breakdown of the calcium-aluminum-silicate phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Ions are released into the solution as a product of the hydrolysis reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium ions are reactants in the chemical equation forming calcium aluminate hydrate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydroxide Ions">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxide Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxide ions establish the alkaline environment necessary for the formation of calcium aluminate hydrate compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Negatively charged ions produced during the hydrolysis reaction, increasing the solution's alkalinity.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxide Ions are released into the solution, indicating an increase in the alkalinity of the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxide ions are reactants that combine with calcium and aluminum species in the reaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Tetrahydroxoaluminate Ions">
  <data key="d0">Tetrahydroxoaluminate Ions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Tetrahydroxoaluminate ions are chemical species formed when aluminum reacts with a strong base, serving as a reactant in precipitation processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Tetrahydroxoaluminate ions are aluminum complexes that react to form the final product.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="C-CaSO4-K-Feldspar Pellets">
  <data key="d0">C-CaSO4-K-Feldspar Pellets</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">C-CaSO4-K-Feldspar Pellets are raw material pellets processed to extract potassium and facilitate carbon dioxide mineralization.&lt;SEP&gt;C-CaSO4-K-Feldspar Pellets are the input material for the extraction and mineralization process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
