<node id="Carbonation">
  <data key="d0">Carbonation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Carbonation is a chemical treatment process applied to solid phases to induce weathering or bubbling reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbonation is a treatment process applied to solid phases, proceeding via weathering or bubbling pathways to produce modified solid products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcination">
  <data key="d0">Calcination</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcination is a thermal treatment and pretreatment process utilized across various industrial and material science applications to modify raw materials, optimize recycling parameters, and enhance overall reactivity. The process is typically conducted under controlled conditions, such as in a nitrogen atmosphere or at specific temperatures like 700°C for three hours, and is frequently analogous to rare earth element ore enrichment. While fundamentally a heating procedure, its specific operational parameters are tailored to the target feedstock and desired chemical outcomes.

The method is applied to a diverse range of materials, including phosphogypsum waste, raw material pellets, feldspar pellets, beneficiated solid phases following chemical treatment, enriched concentrates, and WBS. Depending on the substrate, calcination serves distinct functional purposes: it prepares raw material pellets, releases sulfur dioxide gas from feldspar, acts as an alternative to acidic processing for enriched concentrates, and ensures that raw phosphogypsum is safe for construction use.

Mechanistically, calcination induces dehydration behavior and alters impurity profiles through eutectic processes that facilitate impurity removal. This thermal treatment specifically enables the transformation of soluble phosphate into pyrophosphate and the removal of eutectic phosphorus. Although the process successfully modifies material composition and facilitates reactivity, it is important to note that the thermal nature of calcination carries inherent risks of increasing the overall carbon footprint.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination is a thermal process used to study the dehydration behavior and impurity changes of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination is a thermal treatment process applied to phosphogypsum waste to optimize its recycling parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination is a heating process applied to crushed rock to reduce organic content before acidulation.&lt;SEP&gt;A modification method for phosphogypsum and a key step in producing β-building gypsum powder.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcination is a thermal treatment process where materials are heated to prepare them for clinker formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791207433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methane">
  <data key="d0">Methane</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Methane is a gaseous compound that functions as a significant greenhouse gas with distinct environmental and industrial characteristics. In natural and agricultural settings, it is produced and released within flooded environments through various biogeochemical pathways. As a greenhouse gas, its atmospheric removal rate is notably reduced due to chemical competition with phosphine gas. Furthermore, methane is emitted during the storage of phosphogypsum, a fact documented in reference tables.

Industrially, methane is generated during the gasification of lignite, where it acts as a reactant derived from the coal's volatile components. It serves as a primary component of syngas, and its production is strongly dependent on the concentration of water vapor. During this gasification process, methane also contributes to hydrogen production. These combined roles underscore methane's importance across both ecological cycles and chemical manufacturing processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791119375</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rice Paddy Ecosystem">
  <data key="d0">Rice Paddy Ecosystem</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Rice Paddy Ecosystem is a flooded agricultural environment characterized by distinct soil layers and active methane cycling.&lt;SEP&gt;The Rice Paddy Ecosystem is a flooded soil environment characterized by distinct redox layers that facilitate methane production and consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methanotrophs">
  <data key="d0">Methanotrophs</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Methanotrophs are microorganisms residing in the rhizosphere that biologically consume methane before atmospheric release.&lt;SEP&gt;Methanotrophs are microorganisms located in the rhizosphere that consume methane.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790847976</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aerenchymal Transport">
  <data key="d0">Aerenchymal Transport</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Aerenchymal transport is a biological mechanism that facilitates the movement of methane from submerged soil to the atmosphere.&lt;SEP&gt;Aerenchymal Transport is a plant-mediated mechanism for moving gases like methane through waterlogged soils.&lt;SEP&gt;Aerenchymal transport is a mechanism for methane release from rice paddies to the atmosphere.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="El Zrelli, R.">
  <data key="d0">El Zrelli, R.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">El Zrelli, R. is a researcher who co-authored a 2019 study on radiation hazard assessment of industrial wastes in Tunisia.&lt;SEP&gt;El Zrelli, R. is a researcher who conducted natural radioactivity and radiation hazard assessments of industrial wastes in Gabes.&lt;SEP&gt;El Zrelli, R. is a researcher who conducted natural radioactivity and radiation hazard assessments of industrial wastes in Gabes.&lt;SEP&gt;El Zrelli, R. is a co-author of a 2019 study on natural radioactivity and radiation hazard assessment in Gabes, Tunisia.&lt;SEP&gt;El Zrelli, R. is a researcher who conducted natural radioactivity and radiation hazard assessments of industrial wastes in Gabes.&lt;SEP&gt;El Zrelli, R. is a primary author of the research article on natural radioactivity and radiation hazard assessment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026</data>
