<node id="Ebullition">
  <data key="d0">Ebullition</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Ebullition is a gas transport mechanism involving the physical bursting of gas bubbles from waterlogged soils.&lt;SEP&gt;Ebullition is a physical mechanism involving bubble release that transports methane from soil to the atmosphere.&lt;SEP&gt;Ebullition is the bubbling release of methane gas from anaerobic soils into the atmosphere.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Floodwater">
  <data key="d0">Floodwater</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Floodwater is the water body situated above the soil surface, acting as a medium for gas transport.&lt;SEP&gt;Floodwater is the uppermost layer in a rice paddy ecosystem, situated above the soil profile.&lt;SEP&gt;Floodwater is the top layer in the rice paddy ecosystem with an oxidation-reduction potential greater than 300 mV.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aerobic Layer">
  <data key="d0">Aerobic Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Aerobic Layer is the upper soil zone with high redox potential (Eh &gt; 300 mV) where oxygen is present.&lt;SEP&gt;The aerobic layer is a soil zone in the rice paddy ecosystem characterized by high redox potential (Eh &gt; 300 mV).&lt;SEP&gt;The aerobic layer is a soil stratum in rice paddies with an Eh between 100 and 300 mV.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Facultative Anaerobic Layer">
  <data key="d0">Facultative Anaerobic Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The facultative anaerobic layer is a soil zone in the rice paddy ecosystem with a redox potential starting at 100 mV.&lt;SEP&gt;Facultative Anaerobic Layer is a soil zone with intermediate redox potential (Eh 100 to 300 mV) between aerobic and anaerobic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;The facultative anaerobic layer hosts rhizosphere methanotrophs that consume methane.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rabaoui, L.">
  <data key="d0">Rabaoui, L.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Rabaoui, L. is a co-author of the 2019 study on radiation hazard assessment in Tunisia.&lt;SEP&gt;Rabaoui, L. is a co-author of the 2019 study on industrial waste radiation hazards in Tunisia.&lt;SEP&gt;Rabaoui, L. is a co-author of the research article on natural radioactivity and radiation hazard assessment.</data>
