<node id="Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate, chemically represented by the formula CaSO4·2H2O and commonly known as gypsum, is a stable crystalline compound that serves as the primary chemical and structural component of phosphogypsum. It typically constitutes over 80% of phosphogypsum's composition, alongside other minerals such as quartz, and fundamentally dictates the material's physical and chemical properties. The compound is characterized by its consistent stability, distinct crystal morphology, and a notable absence of initial gelling activity, which collectively define the baseline behavior of phosphogypsum waste streams and play a critical role in their industrial processing and environmental management.

Formed as a crystalline byproduct of acidulation reactions and during setting processes, Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate is frequently studied for its solubility characteristics, particularly in nitric acid and during alkaline treatment, where it acts as the predominant solubilized compound. It is also known to undergo redox reactions within these systems. In analytical and advanced processing workflows, the compound is identified through its characteristic crystal morphology and serves as a standard mineral reference pattern, often visualized with magenta vertical tick marks in diffraction analyses. It can be analyzed via mass spectrometry in conjunction with EDTA and recovered as high-purity gypsum through purification procedures, where it precipitates from post-solubilization filtrates containing calcium-EDTA complexes. Furthermore, the material exhibits a significant environmental and industrial association with rare earth elements, reportedly sequestering between 70% and 80% of the system's total rare earth content.&lt;SEP&gt;The primary chemical compound composing phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate is a mineral phase in phosphogypsum that rarely incorporates radium due to solubility and crystal structure differences.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013</data>
