<node id="Hemihydrate">
  <data key="d0">Hemihydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hemihydrate is formed when Calcium sulfate dihydrate removes 1.5H2O, exhibiting excellent performance for material applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemihydrate is formed when Calcium sulfate dihydrate removes 1.5H2O, exhibiting excellent performance for material applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemihydrate is formed when Calcium sulfate dihydrate removes 1.5H2O, exhibiting excellent performance for material applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Hemihydrate is a mineral form found in the evaporites of water-soluble material from gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A calcium sulfate form that crystallizes during production and forms solid solutions that stabilize the sulfate structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188559</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anhydrous Calcium Sulfate">
  <data key="d0">Anhydrous Calcium Sulfate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Anhydrous calcium sulfate is a processed material derived from thermal-treated phosphogypsum, used in flooring and binder applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrous calcium sulfate is formed when Calcium sulfate dihydrate removes 2H2O, simultaneously eliminating most harmful impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrous calcium sulfate is a processed material derived from thermal-treated phosphogypsum, used in flooring and binder applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrous calcium sulfate is formed when Calcium sulfate dihydrate removes 2H2O, simultaneously eliminating most harmful impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrous calcium sulfate is a processed material derived from thermal-treated phosphogypsum, used in flooring and binder applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Anhydrous calcium sulfate is formed when Calcium sulfate dihydrate removes 2H2O, simultaneously eliminating most harmful impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
