  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Sulfuric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Sulfuric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulfuric acid is a versatile mineral acid and chemical reagent extensively utilized in industrial processing, chemical manufacturing, and resource recovery. It serves as a fundamental reactant in the wet phosphoric acid process, where it decomposes phosphate ores such as apatite, fluorapatite, and general phosphate rock to produce phosphoric acid and phosphogypsum as a byproduct. During this acidulation, the acid specifically attacks fluorapatite and interacts with thorium(IV) phosphate to yield thorium sulfate and phosphoric acid, with concentrated applications known to induce radionuclide fractionation. While the reaction proceeds, sulfuric acid remains in excess within the reaction slurry, a condition that actively controls the shape and size of gypsum crystals. Additionally, some surviving phosphate rock particles resist its attack, and unreacted acid persists as a chemical residue within the pores of the resulting phosphogypsum after filtration, directly contributing to the material's acidic nature.

Beyond its initial consumption, sulfuric acid is intrinsically linked to phosphogypsum through cyclical recovery and synthesis processes. It can be manufactured directly from phosphogypsum, which serves as the primary raw material, via solid-solid reactions or industrial processing that utilizes sulfur dioxide derived from phosphogypsum treatment. Various technologies facilitate this recovery: phosphogypsum co-production technology yields sulfuric acid that is directly reused in phosphoric acid production, while PSC technology recovers it as a high-value chemical byproduct that is entirely reused within the original phosphoric acid unit, significantly contributing to economic revenue. In some production facilities, it is also manufactured as a final product using processed kiln gas. Furthermore, it can be extracted from processing streams via electrodialysis and reintroduced into phosphoric acid manufacturing cycles or redirected for metallurgical applications. In certain regulatory or reporting contexts, it is also documented as an air emission and a listed product.

In secondary applications, sulfuric acid functions as a highly effective leaching agent for extracting valuable metals and rare earth elements from diverse sources, particularly phosphogypsum. It is extensively evaluated as a chemical additive in cycled aqueous solutions to enhance leaching efficiency, enabling the gradual enrichment of rare earth elements and the recovery of phosphorus pentoxide. Notably, it exhibits the lowest gypsum solubility among tested acids, making it a viable alternative for cycle leaching processes and serving as a key chemical component in systems used to model the solubility of gypsum and insoluble anhydrite. Additionally, it is utilized in cement production, where it is generated as a coproduct alongside cement during phosphogypsum utilization. These multifaceted roles reinforce sulfuric acid's status as both a critical industrial input and a highly recoverable resource within chemical and metallurgical systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016</data>
