<node id="Calcium Sulfate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium Sulfate is a chemical and mineral compound that occurs in multiple crystalline forms, specifically gypsum, bassanite, and anhydrite. It serves as the primary constituent of pure gypsum and functions as the main component of phosphogypsum, an impure industrial byproduct generated through the reaction of phosphate ores with sulfuric acid. As the principal calcium source within phosphogypsum, Calcium Sulfate plays a critical role in various industrial and chemical processing applications. Its physicochemical properties are heavily influenced by its source material and processing methods. When derived from phosphogypsum, it exhibits an inversion temperature between 390 and 450°C, which decreases to 370–390°C after purification. The compound is highly soluble in ethylenediaminetetraacetic acid (EDTA), a trait utilized in assessing various metal complexes, and its chemical stability is actively studied for rare earth element recovery, with particular emphasis on europium.

In industrial and materials science contexts, Calcium Sulfate undergoes thermal decomposition and reduction reactions, often being reduced by iron compounds during phosphogypsum processing. It acts as an excellent oxygen carrier and serves as a direct precursor for synthesizing crystalline whiskers. The reduction process ultimately yields a final solid product characterized by a large crystal lattice structure. Analytically, Calcium Sulfate is frequently identified and measured within phosphogypsum samples, with its presence across distinct mineral phases routinely verified, and it is represented in mineral reference patterns by green vertical tick marks.

Beyond its geological and industrial prevalence, Calcium Sulfate is extensively utilized in biomedical and construction materials. It functions as a foundational matrix material and primary component in composite bone cement, while also acting as a minor phase within the initial cement mixture. During the cement setting process, it dissociates to release calcium ions, facilitating the hardening and structural development of the composite. These diverse characteristics underscore the compound's significance across materials science, chemical processing, metallurgical recovery, and biomedical engineering.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate is the crystalline main component of Phosphogypsum, serving as the precursor for whisker preparation.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate is a chemical compound studied in the context of crystallization in phosphoric acid systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate is a compound involved in the primary reaction with coke, producing calcium oxide, sulfur dioxide, and carbon dioxide.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate is a product that can be produced from Phosphogypsum through novel valorization routes.&lt;SEP&gt;The primary raw material in phosphogypsum, represented as $2\text{CaSO}_4$ in the chemical equation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003</data>
