</node>
<node id="Calcite">
  <data key="d0">Calcite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcite is the crystalline form of calcium carbonate produced as the final product of the industrial process.&lt;SEP&gt;A crystalline form of calcium carbonate produced in the carbonation system.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcite is a common solid form in which calcium carbonate is found.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791120814</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="KOH">
  <data key="d0">KOH</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">KOH is a chemical reagent added during the processing step to facilitate the production of Portlandite and Potassium Sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;KOH, or potassium hydroxide, is a chemical reactant used in the thermostatic jacket to convert washed PG into Portlandite.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Raw PG">
  <data key="d0">Raw PG</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Raw PG is the unprocessed phosphogypsum material extracted directly from the phosphate industry.&lt;SEP&gt;Raw PG refers to raw phosphogypsum produced by the phosphate industry before processing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Washed PG">
  <data key="d0">Washed PG</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Washed PG is the purified phosphogypsum material obtained after the washing process removes soluble impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Washed PG is phosphogypsum that has undergone a washing process to remove soluble impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methanogenesis">
  <data key="d0">Methanogenesis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Methanogenesis is a biological process occurring in anaerobic layers where methanogens produce methane.&lt;SEP&gt;Methanogenesis is a biological process occurring in the anaerobic layer of rice paddies where methane is produced from organic matter decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;A biochemical process occurring in the anaerobic layer that produces methane.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Acetogenesis">
  <data key="d0">Acetogenesis</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Acetogenesis is a metabolic pathway in anaerobic conditions that converts substrates into acetate.&lt;SEP&gt;A biochemical process occurring in the anaerobic layer alongside methanogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Acetogenesis is a biological process occurring in the anaerobic layer of rice paddies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Decomposition of Soil Organic Matter">
  <data key="d0">Decomposition of Soil Organic Matter</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Decomposition of Soil Organic Matter is the breakdown process of organic material in lower anaerobic soil layers.&lt;SEP&gt;A breakdown process of organic material that occurs in the deep anaerobic layer.&lt;SEP&gt;Decomposition of soil organic matter occurs in the deep anaerobic layer, providing substrates for methanogenesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Methanogens">
  <data key="d0">Methanogens</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Methanogens are microorganisms residing in anaerobic layers that drive methanogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Methanogens are microorganisms residing in the anaerobic layer of rice paddies that drive the process of methanogenesis.&lt;SEP&gt;Microorganisms present in the anaerobic layer that drive methanogenesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rhizosphere">
  <data key="d0">Rhizosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Rhizosphere is the soil region surrounding plant roots, characterized by microbial activity and methane consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhizosphere is the root zone region whose depth determines the appropriate soil horizon for mechanical processing.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil region surrounding plant roots where biological processes maintain a pH close to 7.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil region surrounding plant roots whose development is hindered by standard technology but improved by intra-soil milling.&lt;SEP&gt;Rhizosphere is the root zone region whose depth determines the appropriate soil horizon for mechanical processing.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil region surrounding plant roots where biological processes maintain a pH close to 7.&lt;SEP&gt;The soil region surrounding plant roots whose development is hindered by standard technology but improved by intra-soil milling.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790950059</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anaerobic Layer">
  <data key="d0">Anaerobic Layer</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Anaerobic Layer is the lower soil zone with negative redox potential where methanogenesis and acetogenesis occur.&lt;SEP&gt;A soil zone characterized by negative redox potential containing methanogens and specific biochemical processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790942862</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Ca3Al2(OH)12">
  <data key="d0">Ca3Al2(OH)12</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ca3Al2(OH)12 is a complex calcium aluminate hydrate that decomposes into calcium hydroxide and other compounds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790848098</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Hydroxide">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Hydroxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium hydroxide, also widely recognized as portlandite, is a chemical compound that serves distinct roles in both carbonation chemistry and industrial waste processing. It is formed through the decomposition of calcium aluminate hydrate, also referred to as calcium aluminum hydroxide, and functions as a key reactant in carbonation processes, specifically appearing at the 58-minute mark. In certain reaction sequences, the compound is stoichiometrically represented as three moles during the initial reaction.

In the context of phosphogypsum management, calcium hydroxide manifests as a specific precipitate derived from phosphogypsum impurities and is routinely recovered from phosphogypsum waste alongside other salts. During the thermal treatment of this waste, the compound actively reacts with freed phosphate ions to produce inactive compounds. Through these varied applications, calcium hydroxide operates as both a decomposition product and an active chemical agent across different industrial and chemical pathways.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium hydroxide is a product formed during the hydrolysis of calcium sulfide in the presence of water.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium hydroxide is a specific precipitate formed from PG impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Hydroxide is a chemical compound formed during the stabilization process.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound with the formula Ca(OH)2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791119375</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pure Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Pure Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Pure Gypsum is a high-purity form of gypsum used as a starting material for the carbonation process.&lt;SEP&gt;A refined starting sample used in the carbonation process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-027</data>
