<node id="Kaolinite">
  <data key="d0">Kaolinite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Kaolinite is a clay mineral that serves as the principal constituent of kaolin and frequently occurs as a minor accessory component in phosphate rock and various other rock formations. In industrial applications, it acts as a critical raw material precursor for the production of metakaolin. Additionally, Kaolinite is utilized in thermal processing, where it is added to phosphogypsum reactions to modify melting characteristics.

From an environmental and chemical standpoint, the mineral demonstrates significant adsorption capabilities, effectively removing fluoride and orthophosphate from aqueous solutions, a process likely driven by the development of a positive surface charge. Furthermore, Kaolinite has been extensively studied for its ability to adsorb rare earth ions, particularly under basic pH conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022</data>
