<node id="Water">
  <data key="d0">Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Water is a fundamental chemical compound that plays critical roles across industrial, laboratory, and material science applications. It functions dually as both a reactant and a product in numerous chemical processes. As a reactant, it is frequently introduced as a variable input into production reaction bowls for gasification, the hydrolysis of calcium aluminum silicate hydroxide, general hydrolysis reactions, the acidulation of fluorapatite, and processes involving sulfuric acid. Conversely, it is generated as a chemical product during the water-gas shift reaction and the hydrolysis of pyrophosphate ions, where it is occasionally represented as three molecules in reaction outputs.

Beyond its reactive capabilities, water serves extensively as a solvent and functional medium. It facilitates analytical and purification procedures, including the dissolution of calcium carbonate and the solubility determination of phosphatic and fluoride compounds, often in conjunction with aqueous citric acid. In radiochemical contexts, it acts as a solvent for Radon-222, with solubility levels influenced by temperature and partition coefficients. Additionally, in certain specialized experimental or nuclear settings, it is characterized as a substance that reduces recoiling atom energy, a property that may increase emanation coefficients while decreasing atmospheric transport.

In industrial and material science applications, water is a raw material consumed by PCR, PBG, and PSC processes. It is added to phosphogypsum during stabilization, functioning as both a natural constituent and an active washing agent to extract impurities from purified samples. Water also drives hydration processes in wet chemical reactions, specifically triggering the immediate conversion of calcium sulfate hemihydrate into gypsum. This hydration capability is leveraged in material science as the setting liquid for bone cement, a role that has necessitated the use of ethanol for displacement measurements in experimental settings. Furthermore, water is recognized as a vital resource that is systematically tracked in environmental impact analyses across all operational scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
