<node id="Thermal Decomposition">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Decomposition</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A reaction type where a compound breaks down into simpler substances, such as calcium hydroxide and aluminum hydroxide.&lt;SEP&gt;Thermal Decomposition is a process mentioned as a possible context for the breakdown of aluminum-containing phases in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A synthesis method involving boiling, drying, and calcining bovine bones at 800 °C to remove organic matter and produce hydroxyapatite.</data>
