<node id="Cementitious Materials">
  <data key="d0">Cementitious Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Cementitious materials are binding construction composites and geotechnical building materials primarily synthesized using phosphogypsum (PG) as a core component or admixture, frequently coupled with industrial solid waste. These materials function as essential elements in construction applications, where the incorporation of phosphogypsum enables the transformation of industrial byproducts into viable building composites. Their development and utilization are deeply embedded within industrial and research frameworks, providing a broader context for studying phosphogypsum and its associated chemical reactions.

In practical and experimental settings, cementitious materials are extensively utilized to evaluate critical performance metrics, particularly durability and mechanical properties. Despite their functional role in construction and waste valorization, they are also characterized economically as low-value-added products generated through PCR technology. Collectively, these materials represent a specialized intersection of construction engineering, industrial waste management, and materials science, highlighting ongoing efforts to optimize phosphogypsum-based composites while acknowledging their current market classification.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008</data>
