<node id="Fluorine">
  <data key="d0">Fluorine</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fluorine is a chemical element that occurs in phosphogypsum primarily as fluorides, with concentrations significantly exceeding Earth's crust averages. In dried phosphogypsum, it comprises approximately 1.17 wt%, while trace measurements in phosphogypsum samples range from 0.01 to 2.24 μg/g. It is typically adsorbed onto phosphogypsum surfaces and functions as a hazardous impurity. During phosphogypsum synthesis, fluorine influences the coprecipitation of calcium and rare earth elements, and it plays a distinct geochemical role by substituting oxygen during the initial step of the SiO2 dissolution mechanism. In industrial contexts such as the CLG process, it migrates and transforms across solid and gas phases. Its concentration is routinely quantified using a fluorine ion selective electrode, and in specific samples like HDS, it appears at lower levels that can be effectively reduced through citric acid treatment.

Due to its toxic and harmful properties, fluorine poses substantial environmental and health risks. Originating from fluoride minerals in phosphogypsum, as well as natural and industrial sources like volcanoes and factories, it readily mobilizes into surrounding environments. Once in aqueous solutions, it acts as a persistent contaminant that forms stable precipitates, complicating natural remediation efforts. Fluorine leaches into soil and aquifer sediments, where its transfer and distribution in soil and plants are actively studied, and it ultimately enters the human body through environmental cycling.

To mitigate these risks, standard industrial protocols prioritize the removal of fluorine during the pretreatment phase of phosphogypsum processing. Advanced remediation strategies include the application of phosphogypsum-derived hydroxyapatite nanoparticles for efficient extraction from contaminated solutions, alongside solidification techniques that immobilize the element within the phosphogypsum matrix to ensure safer long-term storage and disposal, effectively preventing environmental release.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorine is a significant impurity in phosphogypsum that impacts cement setting time and strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorine is an impurity in PG that significantly impacts cement setting time and strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-001</data>
