<node id="Thermal Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Thermal Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermal treatment is a high-temperature processing technique primarily utilized for material synthesis and the modification of various mineral and industrial materials. It serves as a current standard method for treating phosphogypsum and processing phosphate ores, with the primary objective of altering their physical and chemical properties. As a high-temperature process, it is integral to several material synthesis workflows, though its implementation is frequently constrained by significant operational bottlenecks, particularly high energy consumption and the release of volatile components during processing.

In specialized mineral processing applications, thermal treatment is strategically deployed to enhance material characteristics and concentrate valuable elements. When applied to calcined washed beneficiated solids, the process actively promotes the crystallization state of calcium fluoride. Furthermore, in flowsheets involving rare earth extraction, thermal treatment is typically implemented after washing stages to further increase the concentration of rare earth elements within the final concentrate. These targeted applications highlight the technique's versatility in optimizing material composition and structure across diverse industrial contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791118548</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Autoclave Method">
  <data key="d0">Autoclave Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The autoclave method is a traditional synthesis technique for α-Hemihydrate that operates under high temperature and pressure but is limited by equipment and safety constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;The autoclave method is a traditional synthesis technique for α-Hemihydrate that operates under high temperature and pressure but is limited by equipment and safety constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;The autoclave method is a traditional synthesis technique for α-Hemihydrate that operates under high temperature and pressure but is limited by equipment and safety constraints.</data>
