<node id="Table 1">
  <data key="d0">Table 1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 1 serves as a scientific data compilation that encompasses multiple distinct analytical contexts depending on the specific study. In the context of phosphogypsum research, Table 1 functions as a comprehensive reference for chemical processing and environmental analysis. It catalogs phosphogypsum sample codes alongside their industrial sources, while detailing the material's major elemental composition and concentrations as determined by X-ray Fluorescence. Furthermore, it documents the primary physical phases and compositional characteristics identified through X-ray Diffraction and X-ray Fluorescence analyses. The table systematically summarizes various preparation methods and evaluates their specific effects on the production of α-Hemihydrate from phosphogypsum. Additionally, it presents analytical data on macro-ion content within water extracts, organized by varying phosphogypsum application rates and dosages, and provides corresponding macro-ion profiles for Haplic Chernozem soil. Together, these datasets consolidate methodological and analytical information for phosphogypsum-based chemical synthesis and soil-water extract ion profiling.

In a separate context focusing on biomaterials, Table 1 documents the physical characteristics of composite bone cement samples. This version of the table lists density and porosity values for the composites, alongside a structured summary of setting times and physical properties measured across different sodium chloride concentrations. By addressing both phosphogypsum processing and composite cement properties, Table 1 adapts to distinct research domains while maintaining a structured format for reporting key experimental parameters and analytical results.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 1 presents the physicochemical characteristics of the soil and biofertilizer used in the experiments.&lt;SEP&gt;Data table referenced in the text regarding microbial fermentation and material decomposition.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 1 illustrates the typical major element composition of phosphogypsum produced under different processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 1 presents the life cycle inventory analysis detailing resource consumption and energy usage for PCR, PBG, and PSC technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003</data>
