<node id="Zhang et al.">
  <data key="d0">Zhang et al.</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Zhang et al. refers to multiple distinct research groups cited across different scientific domains. One prominent group has focused on environmental and materials science, specifically investigating phosphogypsum utilization and carbon dioxide capture. Their research details the reaction mechanisms of phosphogypsum decomposition slag in the context of CO2 sequestration, highlighting sustainable approaches to industrial waste management and greenhouse gas reduction.

A separate research team, also cited as Zhang et al., has concentrated on mineral processing and hydrometallurgy. This group documented the chemical decomposition of phosphates derived from monazite ore using caustic soda, providing insights into alkaline extraction methods for phosphate recovery.

In a third distinct area of study, another group referenced as Zhang et al. has contributed to agricultural science and horticulture. Their work applied an orthogonal experimental design to systematically optimize fertilizer ratios for blueberry cultivation, aiming to improve crop productivity and nutrient efficiency through structured statistical methodology.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013</data>
