<node id="Cement Retarder">
  <data key="d0">Cement Retarder</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Cement retarder is a construction additive and industrial application material specifically designed to control the setting time of cement and cement mixtures. It functions as a key component in construction applications that utilize various forms of processed gypsum, including modified phosphogypsum, purified phosphogypsum, and high-purity gypsum. By regulating the hydration process, the material ensures optimal workability and structural development during construction projects.

In industrial and environmental contexts, particularly within China, the production and use of cement retarder represent a conventional and established pathway for the recycling of phosphogypsum. This application serves as a commercial and functional solution for high-purity gypsum derivatives, effectively transforming industrial byproducts into valuable construction materials while supporting sustainable waste management practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement retarder is a functional application in cement production where phosphogypsum serves as a substitute for natural gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Cement retarder is a basic utilization method for Phosphogypsum in the construction industry.&lt;SEP&gt;A product generated by the PCR process, with a production quantity of 1030.00 kg.</data>
