<node id="PG">
  <data key="d0">PG</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">PG, commonly known as Phosphogypsum, is an environmentally hazardous industrial byproduct and solid waste that serves as a foundational raw sample material across diverse scientific and engineering research fields. Chemically, it is predominantly composed of calcium sulfate dihydrate, functioning as a complex matrix that also incorporates minor compounds such as calcium fluoride (CaF2), along with fluorine and phosphorus elements. This material is notably enriched with rare earth elements (REEs) and rare and precious heavy metals, with the distribution of REEs heavily influenced by their specific ionic properties and the crystalline structure of the host material. Due to its hazardous environmental impact and valuable constituent elements, PG is actively targeted for solubilization and resource utilization. Processing and recovery mechanisms rely on dissolution, decomposition, and crystallization processes, with researchers routinely analyzing its thermal behaviors, elemental composition, and rare earth oxide content to mitigate environmental risks while efficiently extracting valuable components through controlled chemical transformations.

In addition to its resource recovery potential, PG is frequently utilized as a dried sample type for radionuclide concentration measurements, as it exhibits significant radioactive disequilibrium characterized by notable deviations from natural isotopic ratios. The material also finds practical application in geotechnical engineering, where it is incorporated into cemented paste backfill (CPB) mixtures. For this specific application, PG typically requires pretreatment to remove impurities before integration.

Furthermore, PG has emerged as a critical industrial material in energy conversion processes, specifically serving as an oxygen carrier or foundational support material for various compound oxygen carriers in the chemical looping gasification (CLG) of low-rank lignite to produce syngas. In this context, its strong oxygen-carrying capacity is leveraged, and its grain growth is deliberately inhibited by silicon dioxide (SiO2) to maintain stable oxygen-carrying properties. Throughout these gasification studies, PG is recognized as the primary mineral material undergoing catalytic and reduction-oxidation decomposition, making it a central focus for understanding its physicochemical characteristics and transformation mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;PG is an environmentally harmful solid waste containing rare earth elements and rare and precious heavy metals.&lt;SEP&gt;PG (Phosphogypsum) is a byproduct whose resource utilization involves dissolution, decomposition, and crystallization mechanisms.&lt;SEP&gt;PG is a material utilized in integrated technologies, reacting with coke during calcination.&lt;SEP&gt;PG is an industrial byproduct whose disposal and resource utilization are analyzed for environmental and economic impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;PG refers to phosphogypsum, a material whose future management is the central focus of the study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-012</data>
