<node id="Monazite">
  <data key="d0">Monazite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Monazite is a phosphate crystal mineral and a primary ore source of rare earth elements, thorium, and uranium oxides. Chemically, it contains phosphates that can be decomposed through the application of caustic soda. Geographically, this mineral is notably found in Florida, with specific deposits located at Green Cove Springs.

Beyond its role as a valuable source of critical metals, Monazite serves as a benchmark and reference material for evaluating the potential economic value of phosphogypsum and for typical rare metal content levels. In industrial processing contexts, it appears as a stable mineral phase where rare earth elements occur independently within phosphogypsum, and it is also identified as an undissolved, independent rare earth element mineral inclusion found in leaching residues. Additionally, Monazite exhibits distinct radiological properties, with its Radon-222 emanation coefficient measured between 0.5% and 25%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016</data>
