<node id="Lime">
  <data key="d0">Lime</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lime is a versatile chemical additive and activator primarily utilized in the treatment and valorization of phosphogypsum. In industrial and construction applications, lime is combined with phosphogypsum and fly ash to significantly enhance the strength and durability of phosphogypsum-based road materials. It functions as an alkaline activator that promotes hydration reactions when used alongside fly ash and other supplementary materials. Chemically, lime serves as a reagent that reacts with soluble phosphorus and fluorine present in phosphogypsum, effectively converting them into insoluble compounds to mitigate environmental risks.

Beyond civil engineering, lime is also employed as an agricultural supplement to treat phosphogypsum, preparing it for safe use in soil amendment applications. Through these multifaceted roles, lime facilitates the chemical stabilization, structural improvement, and environmental remediation of phosphogypsum across both construction and agricultural sectors.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime is a chemical reagent added to phosphogypsum to react with soluble phosphorus and fluorine, forming insoluble compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime is an additive used with fly ash to enhance the strength and durability of phosphogypsum-based road materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime is an alternative name for Calcium Oxide, produced in the carbothermal reduction reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Lime (CaO) is a useful byproduct generated from the conversion of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791209349</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Rare Earths">
  <data key="d0">Rare Earths</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Rare earths are elements leached from phosphogypsum following hydrothermal conversion processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Rare earths are critical materials whose global market supply disruptions were modeled in a 2021 research study.&lt;SEP&gt;Rare earths are elements leached from phosphogypsum following hydrothermal conversion processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Rare earths are critical materials whose global market supply disruptions were modeled in a 2021 research study.&lt;SEP&gt;Rare earths are elements leached from phosphogypsum following hydrothermal conversion processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Rare earths are critical materials whose global market supply disruptions were modeled in a 2021 research study.</data>
