<node id="Apatite">
  <data key="d0">Apatite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Apatite is a versatile mineral group characterized by variable physical, chemical, and crystallographic properties, commonly occurring as carbonate apatite within phosphorite deposits. It serves as the principal phosphate mineral in most phosphate rock deposits and functions as the primary raw material treated with sulfuric acid to produce phosphoric acid. Geologically, apatite's crystal structure readily incorporates trace elements such as uranium and thorium through substitution or adsorption, while also acting as a valuable source for recovering fluorine, strontium, and rare earth elements. Notably, due to the ionic size similarity between radium and calcium, radium frequently substitutes for calcium within the apatite lattice, resulting in measured Radon-222 emanation coefficients ranging from 0.5% to 25%.

Beyond its industrial and geological significance, apatite plays a critical role in biomedical applications. When bioactive biomaterials or composite bone cements are implanted in the body or immersed in Simulated Body Fluid (SBF), a bone-like mineral layer composed of apatite crystals precipitates on their surfaces. This precipitation process is fundamental to the bioactivity of these materials, enabling effective osseointegration and tissue bonding in medical contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003</data>
