<node id="Iron Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Iron Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron oxide is a chemical compound that plays a notable role in phosphate-related materials and industrial processing streams. In its natural state, it serves as a minor mineral component, constituting approximately one percent of the overall composition of phosphorite. During the beneficiation and processing of phosphate ores, iron oxide behaves as a co-occurring compound; its concentration notably increases in the resulting beneficiated concentrates alongside rare earth elements.

Beyond raw ores and processed concentrates, iron oxide is also commonly present as an impurity in phosphogypsum, a byproduct of phosphate manufacturing. In this context, it contributes significantly to the material's complex chemical composition. Together, these characteristics highlight iron oxide's persistent presence across raw phosphate minerals, processed concentrates, and industrial byproducts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001</data>
