<node id="Hydroxyapatite">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxyapatite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydroxyapatite is a calcium phosphate compound and nanocrystalline bioceramic material widely recognized across scientific and industrial domains. Often abbreviated as HAP, it is formally cataloged in mineral reference patterns by red vertical tick marks. Chemically, it can substitute for fluorides within fluorapatite structures and exhibits negative surface charges that actively initiate apatite formation.

The synthesis and formation of Hydroxyapatite vary according to feedstock and environmental conditions. It is manufactured from phosphogypsum through hydrothermal processing, derived from bovine bone waste, or precipitates in situ during the immobilization of phosphorus within CPB mixtures. In certain engineered formulations, it is compounded with calcium sulfate to optimize its functional characteristics.

Owing to its biocompatibility, bioactivity, porosity, and structural stability, Hydroxyapatite is extensively deployed in biomedical and materials engineering applications. It functions as a primary structural component and reinforcing phase in composite bone cements and dental implants. Additionally, it remains a central focus in bone tissue engineering, bone repair, cement reinforcement, and nanocomposite development, with continuous research dedicated to refining its preparation methods, material properties, and clinical utility.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite is a calcium phosphate compound identified as a solid product in the reaction process.&lt;SEP&gt;A black base component in the product stack, identified as the largest component at higher PG to lignite ratios.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydroxyapatite is a nanocrystalline material synthesized from phosphogypsum via hydrothermal methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010</data>
