<node id="Fig. 4">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 4</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 4 is a figure label that appears across multiple independent scientific studies, each utilizing the designation to represent a distinct data visualization or diagram related to phosphogypsum and phosphate rock analysis. Because the same identifier is applied to different figures in separate contexts, the provided descriptions collectively refer to four distinct visualizations rather than a single unified image.

In the first context, Fig. 4 illustrates the common extraction technologies and outlines the primary procedural steps required to recover rare earth elements from phosphogypsum. In a second context, it presents soil chemistry data by depicting the equilibrium concentration of macro-ion free forms in soil solution following phosphogypsum application. A third distinct version focuses on radiometric analysis, visualizing the activity ratios of U-238/Ra-226 and U-238/Pb-210 within both phosphate rock and phosphogypsum samples. Finally, a fourth variation serves as a tabular data visualization that catalogs the chemical compositions of phosphogypsum sourced from various countries. Together, these separate figures highlight the diverse analytical, environmental, and industrial applications associated with phosphogypsum research.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 4 presents data on the leaching efficiency of Rare Earth Elements from Phosphogypsum using different acids and reaction conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure displaying SEM micrographs and EDS data of the composite cements using surface mode imaging.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure displaying SEM micrographs of the composite bone cement samples at different magnifications.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 4 displays EDS data with area mode analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 4 illustrates the characterization of phosphogypsum using scanning electron microscopy and X-ray diffraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 4 is a figure displaying the common extraction technology and main steps for recovering rare earth elements from phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010</data>
