  <data key="d0">Hydrogen</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrogen is a gaseous product produced during the gasification of lignite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen is a gaseous product produced during the gasification of lignite.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen is a chemical element whose atom count is balanced on both sides of the reaction equation.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen is a chemical element shown in the molecular diagram of PTEs.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen is a component of syngas whose production is strongly dependent on the amount of water vapors.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen is a key gaseous product produced via the reaction of carbon with water vapor and the gasification of lignite volatile components.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrogen is a gaseous product produced during the gasification of lignite.</data>
