<node id="Elsevier">
  <data key="d0">Elsevier</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">Elsevier is a publishing organization and the parent company of the Academic Press imprint. As a publishing house, it has released a diverse range of academic and technical works, including the book Hydrometallurgy of Rare Earths, a book chapter on sustainable remediation using low-carbon cement, and a 2020 publication dedicated to sustainable remediation.

Beyond general publishing, Elsevier manages the intellectual property and distribution rights for specialized scientific research. The organization holds the copyright for several cited studies on phosphogypsum and environmental research, particularly focusing on phosphogypsum valorization in construction materials. Additionally, Elsevier serves as the official publisher that grants permission for the reprinting of these specific phosphogypsum-related studies.&lt;SEP&gt;Elsevier is a publishing house that released the book Hydrometallurgy of Rare Earths.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-020</data>
