<node id="Dissolution">
  <data key="d0">Dissolution</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Dissolution is a process where PG dissolves in water or solvent, accelerated by physical conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Dissolution is a process where PG dissolves in water or solvent, accelerated by physical conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Dissolution is a chemical process where phosphogypsum mixed with caustic liquid waste is dissolved to separate liquid and solid phases.&lt;SEP&gt;Dissolution is the process where solid precipitates break down into ions within the aqueous phase.&lt;SEP&gt;Dissolution refers to the breakdown of the gypsum matrix and surface particles during the leaching process.&lt;SEP&gt;Dissolution is a process where PG dissolves in water or solvent, accelerated by physical conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Dissolution is the process where calcium carbonate breaks down into ions in an aqueous solution.</data>
