<node id="Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Temperature is a fundamental physicochemical quantity and environmental factor that serves as a critical variable across diverse scientific and industrial applications. Quantitatively, it is a metric measured in Kelvin, typically ranging from 373 to 1573, and is commonly used on the X-axis in analytical plots.

In mineralogical and chemical processes, Temperature supplies the essential thermal energy required to drive phase transformations and facilitate the emergence of distinct chemical compounds. Within these systems, it directly governs the kinetics and morphology of gypsum crystal growth, dictating both the crystallization rate and the final crystal form.

In biological and waste management contexts, particularly composting, Temperature functions as a vital environmental factor that regulates microbial reproduction and bacterial distribution. It is routinely monitored daily to maintain optimal processing conditions, as its characteristic trajectory—rising to a peak before gradually declining—serves as a reliable physicochemical indicator of microbial growth trends and overall biological activity within the compost matrix.&lt;SEP&gt;Temperature is a physical factor that inversely affects the solubility of Radon-222 in water.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-031&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188835</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
