<node id="Heavy Metals">
  <data key="d0">Heavy Metals</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Heavy Metals are toxic and potentially hazardous metallic elements that function as significant environmental contaminants and soil pollutants across various ecosystems. They originate from diverse sources, including agricultural inputs, industrial waste, the natural lithosphere, and notably as adsorbed impurities or trace contaminants within phosphogypsum and other phosphate industry materials. Once introduced into the environment, these elements accumulate in soil and biomass, posing substantial risks to ecological integrity and human health. Their environmental behavior is complex; mobility, plant uptake, and penetration into trophic chains are heavily influenced by soil water regimes, matrix potential, thermodynamic states, and the high solubility of phosphogypsum, which facilitates their diffusion into surrounding water and soil. Specific elements, such as cadmium and zinc, are frequently highlighted in ecological risk assessments. The association and binding characteristics of these metals in soil solutions are typically quantified using the association coefficient, while their spatial distribution and migration patterns in abandoned phosphogypsum deposits are evaluated through techniques like electrical resistivity tomography and multivariate analysis. Furthermore, heavy metals adsorbed by nano-mineral particles face an increased risk of global environmental diffusion, and their concentrations in farming soils are often directly influenced by nearby phosphogypsum piles.

To mitigate these harmful effects and prevent long-term migration, comprehensive management strategies are employed. These contaminants are routinely targeted for removal during pretreatment phases, particularly when extracted from phosphogypsum, where they may be released to form stable precipitates. Remediation efforts frequently involve solidification, passivation into processed soil layers or solutions, and chemical treatments designed to restrict entry into food webs. By effectively immobilizing these toxic elements, it becomes possible to ensure environmental safety, facilitate the environmentally sound recycling of contaminated materials, and safeguard broader ecological systems. Continuous monitoring and rigorous pretreatment remain essential practices to manage Heavy Metals, ensuring that their presence in soil and biomass does not compromise ecological or human health.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy metals are impurities adsorbed on phosphogypsum that are targeted for removal during pretreatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy metals are impurities released from PG that form stable precipitates.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy Metals are harmful components found in phosphogypsum that require solidification to prevent migration over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy metals are contaminants whose behavior in abandoned phosphogypsum deposits is assessed using electrical resistivity tomography and multivariate analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Heavy metals are chemical elements whose mobility in acidic seepage waters is reduced by buffering from alkaline subsoils and groundwaters.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019</data>
