<node id="Phosphorus">
  <data key="d0">Phosphorus</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphorus is a fundamental chemical element that serves a dual role as an essential plant nutrient critical for global food security and a significant environmental contaminant. As a vital nutrient, its solubilization by microorganisms enhances biofertilizer efficacy, and it can be supplied by materials like phosphogypsum, where high application rates significantly increase available soil phosphorus. Conversely, when present in industrial byproducts such as phosphogypsum, phosphorus acts as a toxic and harmful impurity. It is highly enriched in this material, with mass fractions typically ranging from 0.030% to 2.980%, representing residual phosphate from fertilizer production and serving as a key identifier for phosphogypsum in analyzed materials. It correlates with specific particle shapes and is readily detected analytically as a significant peak around 2.0 keV.

Uncontrolled releases of phosphorus from phosphogypsum stockpiles or industrial sites, particularly during rainfall events, lead to its migration into adjacent waterways and aquatic reservoirs. In these environments, it forms stable precipitates, alters authigenic content, and disrupts the global phosphorus cycle. This mobility triggers eutrophication and poses substantial ecological hazards, making phosphorus a focal point of research concerning lake sedimentation and fertilizer industry waste. To mitigate these environmental risks, phosphorus is specifically targeted for removal during pretreatment stages and is effectively immobilized through solidification and stabilization techniques. These methods include incorporating it into cemented paste backfill mixtures via calcium-phosphate species and hydration products, or facilitating its coprecipitation with metallic elements like aluminum and iron.

Beyond waste management, phosphorus is integral to resource recovery and chemical processing. It can be successfully extracted and precipitated from incinerated sewage sludge ash and phosphogypsum. During thermal and chemical treatments, the element undergoes sequential conversion and phase transitions, ultimately remaining in the solid phase residue. Its concentration is routinely quantified using automated wet chemistry analyzers, and its reactivity strictly adheres to chemical stoichiometry, necessitating precise atom balancing in reaction equations. Collectively, these characteristics underscore phosphorus as a foundational element that demands rigorous handling, precise analytical monitoring, and strategic management across industrial, environmental, and chemical applications to balance resource utility with ecological safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus is a significant impurity in phosphogypsum that impacts cement setting time and strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphorus is an impurity in PG that significantly impacts cement setting time and strength.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-033&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-00