<node id="Calcium Fluoride">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Fluoride</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium fluoride (CaF₂) is a chemical compound that primarily manifests as an insoluble solid precipitate during the purification and solubilization of phosphogypsum (PG), as well as during the acidification of rock phosphate with sulfuric acid. It originates from impurities present in PG and emerges through chemical transformations inherent to these processing stages. Within the context of solid beneficiation, calcium fluoride serves as a major crystallized component in Beneficiated Solid, Washed Beneficiated Solid (WBS), and Calcined Washed Beneficiated Solid (TWBS). Its crystallization state is notably enhanced through thermal treatment.

Analytically, the compound is readily identified via X-ray diffraction (XRD) analysis, characterized by prominent diffraction peaks labeled F at approximately 29° and 48°. Furthermore, calcium fluoride demonstrates a moderately complexed interaction with EDTA, which indicates a non-total complexation behavior. Historically and industrially, calcium fluoride has been recognized as a high-value product, drawing significant research attention in studies focused on converting phosphogypsum, particularly through processes involving hydrofluoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;A fluoride compound detected in the studied samples.&lt;SEP&gt;An insoluble solid-phase compound (CaF2) that attaches to the oxygen carrier surface and does not participate in the reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;A molecule depicted as a green sphere bonded to two light blue spheres, present in the starting materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium fluoride is a specific precipitate formed from PG impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Fluoride is a chemical compound present in the final stabilized material.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical compound with the formula CaF2.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-029&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-011</data>
