<node id="Calcium Sulfate Hemihydrate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfate Hemihydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium sulfate hemihydrate is a chemical compound whose transformation to gypsum was analyzed using advanced microscopy techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate hemihydrate is a chemical compound whose transformation to gypsum was analyzed using advanced microscopy techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;A medicine-grade starting material mixed with hydroxyapatite and sodium chloride to form the composite bone cement.&lt;SEP&gt;The precursor compound that reacts with water to form gypsum during the cement setting reaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate hemihydrate is a precursor compound that dissolves and undergoes saturation to form dihydrate crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate hemihydrate is a chemical compound whose transformation to gypsum was analyzed using advanced microscopy techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Sulfate Hemihydrate is a mineral phase in phosphogypsum that has a higher chance of co-precipitating Radium-226 compared to the dihydrate form.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013</data>
