<node id="Particle Size Distribution">
  <data key="d0">Particle Size Distribution</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Particle Size Distribution is a fundamental physical property and analytical data characteristic of phosphogypsum that describes the range and proportion of particle sizes within the material. It functions simultaneously as a critical analytical characterization technique and a dataset used to study phosphogypsum, specifically by quantifying the size range of particles present in the initial sample. This dual role allows researchers to accurately assess the material's structural composition and physical behavior.

In phosphogypsum applications, the particle size distribution typically indicates that the majority of particles fall within the range of 10 to 900 micrometers, with some assessments extending the upper bound to 1000 micrometers. This distribution directly influences key material properties, most notably the permeability of the phosphogypsum matrix. By providing a detailed breakdown of particle dimensions, Particle Size Distribution serves as an essential metric for evaluating the material's physical structure and functional performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-001</data>
