  <data key="d0">Moisture Content</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Moisture content is the water percentage in phosphogypsum, ranging from 5 to 28 percent, which causes particle agglomeration.&lt;SEP&gt;Moisture content is the water percentage in phosphogypsum, ranging from 5 to 28 percent, which causes particle agglomeration.&lt;SEP&gt;Moisture content is a data attribute of PG ranging from 8wt% to 30wt%, influenced by draining duration and local weather conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Moisture content is the water percentage in phosphogypsum, ranging from 5 to 28 percent, which causes particle agglomeration.</data>
