<node id="Portland Cement">
  <data key="d0">Portland Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Portland cement is a widely used traditional and standard binding material in construction, frequently employed in cement pastes and building applications. It is extensively studied for its setting behavior and mechanical properties, often serving as a baseline for research involving various supplementary additives. One prominent area of investigation involves its interaction with phosphogypsum, a byproduct that is increasingly explored for industrial valorization. When incorporated into Portland cement, phosphogypsum can serve multiple roles: weathered phosphogypsum functions as a set retarder, while purified phosphogypsum can be utilized as a raw material during manufacture or as an additive.

The impact of phosphogypsum on the cement's performance varies significantly based on its purity and dosage. Impure or weathered forms tend to retard setting times and reduce compressive strength. Conversely, when purified phosphogypsum is used at low replacement contents, it can enhance or benefit the material's properties. Additionally, Portland cement is frequently examined in combination with other industrial byproducts, such as ground granulated blast furnace slag, which is sometimes used to partially substitute it in experimental studies. Overall, the integration of phosphogypsum into Portland cement represents a dynamic field of research aimed at optimizing construction materials while promoting sustainable waste utilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement is a common building material whose hydration process is affected by soluble components in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement is a binding material where weathered phosphogypsum is utilized as a set retarder.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland Cement is a construction material produced alongside sulfuric acid in the PG-based co-production technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland cement is the final construction material produced using calcium oxide derived from PSC technology.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-001</data>
