<node id="Anhydrite">
  <data key="d0">Anhydrite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Anhydrite is a calcium sulfate mineral compound that primarily composes phosphogypsum, an industrial byproduct. It is commonly present in phosphogypsum alongside other calcium sulfate species and can be prepared or isolated from this material. The formation and development of Anhydrite within this context are notably influenced by the presence of phosphorus and fluorine impurities, which play a critical role in its crystallization and chemical behavior.

Due to its abundance in phosphogypsum, Anhydrite represents a significant component in industrial mineral processing and waste management applications. Its properties and prevalence are directly tied to the specific impurity profile of the source material, making it a key subject in the study of calcium sulfate phases and the utilization of phosphogypsum byproducts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791118208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Egypt">
  <data key="d0">Egypt</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Egypt is a country and geographic region that serves as the foundational location for a series of industrial and scientific investigations centered on phosphate processing and waste management. It is specifically recognized as the site of the Abu-Zaabal phosphate plant, an industrial facility dedicated to phosphoric acid production. Within this national context, extensive research has been conducted, including studies on lanthanide recovery and associated radioactivity assessments. The country is also the primary location for the sampling and comprehensive chemical analysis of phosphogypsum waste.

Researchers have systematically tabulated the chemical compositions of these phosphogypsum samples, focusing on determining the mean weight percentages of various chemical oxides. Data derived from these analyses are prominently featured in scientific charts, where Egypt is represented on the vertical axis with a specific weight percentage measurement of approximately 38%. Overall, Egypt functions as both the geographic origin of key phosphate rock sources and the operational base for facilities and studies examining the chemical, radiological, and material properties of phosphate-related byproducts.&lt;SEP&gt;Egypt is a geographic location associated with phosphate rock sources and lanthanide recovery research.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791118309</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Morocco">
  <data key="d0">Morocco</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Morocco is a sovereign country and geographic region that plays a central role in the scientific study, industrial management, and environmental monitoring of phosphate-related materials. The nation is recognized for its extensive phosphate rock reserves, which include significant sedimentary and igneous occurrences, and hosts major extraction sites such as the Bou Craa phosphate rock deposit. Within these geological formations, phosphate rock contains a rare earth element concentration ranging from 0.14% to 0.16%. The country also houses critical industrial infrastructure, including phosphoric acid plants and the Jorf Lasfar phosphogypsum source.

Phosphogypsum, a primary byproduct of phosphate processing, is extensively analyzed and managed in Morocco. The country is identified as having a high number of phosphogypsum stacks and ponds where contaminated phosphogypsum is stored, prompting ongoing research into industrial byproduct management, environmental impact assessments, and the broader ecological consequences of phosphate mining. Scientific literature frequently references Morocco for the collection and analysis of phosphogypsum samples, with studies tabulating chemical compositions and determining mean weight percentages of chemical oxides. Additionally, Morocco serves as a key geographic reference for environmental and geochemical monitoring, particularly in research examining natural radioactivity within phosphates and phosphogypsum, as well as soil cadmium concentration data. In specific analytical datasets and charts, Morocco is also represented with a weight percentage of approximately 43%.&lt;SEP&gt;Morocco is the geographic region associated with research on recovering chemicals from phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Morocco is a geographic location associated with studies on natural radioactivity in phosphates and phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Morocco is a country in North Africa that hosts the Djorf Lasfar plant.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188835</data>
