  <data key="d0">Soluble Fluorine</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Soluble fluorine is a harmful impurity in phosphogypsum that reacts with lime to form insoluble compounds but can slowly dissolve over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Soluble fluorine is a harmful impurity in phosphogypsum that reacts with lime to form insoluble compounds but can slowly dissolve over time.&lt;SEP&gt;Soluble fluorine is an impurity present in high-purity gypsum, limited to less than 0.015 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;Soluble fluorine is an impurity present in the recovered gypsum, measured at less than 0.015 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;Soluble fluorine is a harmful impurity in phosphogypsum that reacts with lime to form insoluble compounds but can slowly dissolve over time.</data>
