  <data key="d0">Gypsum Plaster</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum plaster is a construction material produced through the recycling and calcination of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum plaster is a construction material produced through the recycling and calcination of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum plaster is a building material whose manufacture can utilize purified phosphogypsum as a raw material.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum plaster is a construction material whose physical properties are detailed across different design formulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum Plaster is a building material produced from purified phosphogypsum, exhibiting reduced normal consistency and increased strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum plaster is a product manufactured by recycling phosphogypsum, with production efficiency dependent on calcination temperature.&lt;SEP&gt;Gypsum plaster is a construction material produced through the recycling and calcination of phosphogypsum.</data>
