<node id="Journal of Hazardous Materials">
  <data key="d0">Journal of Hazardous Materials</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Journal of Hazardous Materials is a scientific and academic journal that publishes research focused on environmental hazards, waste management, and radiological safety. The journal features research on converting waste phosphogypsum into nanoparticles for environmental applications, alongside studies addressing radiological risk and phosphogypsum-amended soil.

It also covers investigations into radioactivity contents in dicalcium phosphate and associated radiological risks. Furthermore, the publication includes work on environmental remediation strategies, such as research on phytostabilisation efficiency in contaminated soils. Through these diverse studies, the Journal of Hazardous Materials serves as a key resource for advancing scientific knowledge on hazardous materials and their ecological impacts.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal of Hazardous Materials is a journal publishing research on tomato trace element uptake in 2014.&lt;SEP&gt;Journal of Hazardous Materials features research on converting waste phosphogypsum into nanoparticles for environmental applications.</data>
