<node id="XRD">
  <data key="d0">XRD</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">X-ray Diffraction (XRD) is an analytical characterization and measurement technique primarily employed for phase identification and structural analysis of solid materials. In industrial and research contexts, it is extensively utilized to study, characterize, and confirm the main phase composition of phosphogypsum waste. The method is also applied to verify the phase identification of mixed powders, particularly as a preliminary step before composite cement preparation.

Beyond general mineralogical assessment, XRD enables the observation of specific diffraction peaks, such as those corresponding to sodium chloride, allowing researchers to correlate spectral data with precise weight percentage measurements. Furthermore, the technique is instrumental in determining the exact crystal structure of specialized composite materials, including nickel/phosphogypsum compound oxygen carriers. Through these varied applications, XRD provides critical insights into the chemical and crystalline properties of phosphogypsum and related industrial compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;XRD is an analytical characterization technique used to study phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791120018</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="XRF">
  <data key="d0">XRF</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">XRF is an analytical characterization technique used to study phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;XRF is an analytical characterization technique used to study phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;XRF is the abbreviation for X-ray Fluorescence, the analytical method used for elemental analysis of PG waste.&lt;SEP&gt;XRF is an analytical measurement technique used alongside XRD and IR to determine the phase composition of phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;XRF is an analytical characterization technique used to study phosphogypsum.</data>
