</node>
<node id="Iron(III) Oxide">
  <data key="d0">Iron(III) Oxide</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron(III) oxide is a chemical and mineral compound that appears across multiple analytical and industrial contexts. In phosphogypsum, it is consistently identified as a trace impurity component found alongside other transition metals. Concentration measurements in this matrix range from 89.10 to 102.60 ppm, and its presence is routinely documented in compositional analysis tables.

In contrast, when evaluated in WBS and TWBS samples, Iron(III) oxide is classified as a main metal element compound. Additionally, in materials science applications, it functions as an iron oxide compound within composite oxygen carriers. In this specific role, it participates in the oxygen release pathway and exhibits a defined release priority.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron(III) oxide is a chemical compound present in phosphogypsum composition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-002</data>
