<node id="Cadmium Ion">
  <data key="d0">Cadmium Ion</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Cadmium Ion (Cd²⁺) is a heavy metal ion that functions as a significant soil contaminant and exists primarily as a free ion within soil solutions. As the active chemical species in this environment, its molar fraction remains lower than the total cadmium content present. The equilibrium concentration and activity of the Cadmium Ion are routinely calculated and analyzed in soil solutions, where its various chemical forms are closely monitored.

In soil environments, the Cadmium Ion frequently binds to form associates, and its overall activity is notably reduced through complexation with other ions and hydroxo complexes. To quantify these interactions, a detailed association coefficient equation is specifically applied to the Cadmium Ion. Furthermore, the environmental mobility and subsequent transfer of the Cadmium Ion to plants are heavily dependent on soil pH levels and the presence of soil carbonates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790950367</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydroxo Complex">
  <data key="d0">Hydroxo Complex</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Hydroxo Complex (CdOH+) is a form of cadmium that binds prematurely in the soil solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical complex formed by cadmium ions that influences their activity and speciation in soil solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A primary form of cadmium in soil solution that drives biogeochemical passivation and reduces cadmium penetration into plants.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hydroxo Complex (CdOH+) is a form of cadmium that binds prematurely in the soil solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical complex formed by cadmium ions that influences their activity and speciation in soil solution.&lt;SEP&gt;A primary form of cadmium in soil solution that drives biogeochemical passivation and reduces cadmium penetration into plants.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790950367</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Carbonate Form">
  <data key="d0">Carbonate Form</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The Carbonate Form (CdCO3^0) is a chemical species of cadmium present in lower concentrations than the hydroxo complex.&lt;SEP&gt;The Carbonate Form (CdCO3^0) is a chemical species of cadmium present in lower concentrations than the hydroxo complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790951494</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
