<node id="BGT* Methodology">
  <data key="d0">BGT* Methodology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The BGT* Methodology is a comprehensive framework that integrates mechanical and chemical strategies for advanced soil engineering and management. Mechanically, it provides a systematic approach for synthesizing specialized devices designed for intra-soil mechanical processing. The development and application of these devices have been rigorously validated through both controlled laboratory experiments and practical field settings, ensuring their operational reliability and effectiveness in real-world contexts.

Chemically, the BGT* Methodology functions as an innovative engineering framework aimed at developing techniques to mitigate critical soil degradation issues. It specifically addresses challenges related to soil pH reduction while prioritizing the maintenance and restoration of optimal soil structure. Additionally, it operates as a transcendental remediation and reclamation technology that effectively facilitates the recycling and management of phosphogypsum. By unifying these mechanical processing capabilities with targeted chemical engineering solutions, the BGT* Methodology delivers a holistic approach to sustainable soil rehabilitation, structural integrity, and industrial byproduct utilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790949590</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
