<node id="Kalinichenko">
  <data key="d0">Kalinichenko</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Kalinichenko is a researcher whose work primarily focuses on soil engineering and environmental chemistry. He holds patents related to intra-soil processing and the simultaneous application of matter, and has co-authored numerous publications detailing these innovations. His research portfolio extensively covers matrix potential, heavy metal behavior in soil, and broader soil engineering applications.

In addition to his practical and experimental work, Kalinichenko is academically recognized for his contributions to theoretical modeling. He is specifically cited for the thermodynamic mathematical model ION-3, which has been referenced in subsequent scientific literature. Collectively, his patents, publications, and theoretical frameworks establish him as a notable figure in soil science and applied thermodynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009</data>
