<node id="USA">
  <data key="d0">USA</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The USA is a sovereign nation that serves as a significant geographic hub for critical mineral resources. It hosts major phosphate rock deposits, specifically encompassing the North Carolina and Florida locations frequently referenced in geological and industrial texts. The extraction and processing of these phosphate reserves make the USA a primary source region for phosphogypsum, a byproduct material that is subject to specific storage conditions within the country.

Beyond its natural resource profile, the USA is a central base for prominent scientific and technological enterprises. It is the country of origin for leading analytical instrument manufacturers, including ThermoFisher and Agilent. Additionally, the nation hosts StatSoft, a recognized software company. Together, these attributes underscore the USA's dual role as a key location for both phosphate-related material production and advanced analytical instrumentation development.&lt;SEP&gt;The USA is the country containing the Black Hills Region study site.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791142316</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Haplic Chernozem">
  <data key="d0">Haplic Chernozem</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Haplic Chernozem is a world-famous South-European facies soil type primarily situated in the northern Rostov Region of South Russia. This soil is characterized by distinct physical and chemical properties, although it has notably experienced significant degradation over time. Its unique composition and regional prevalence have made it a subject of considerable scientific interest and environmental management efforts.

In contemporary research, Haplic Chernozem is frequently employed as the primary substrate for model experiments focused on phosphogypsum application and remediation. These studies utilize the soil to evaluate environmental interventions, specifically analyzing shifts in macro-ion content and investigating the various chemical forms of cadmium within the treated substrate. Consequently, Haplic Chernozem serves as a critical reference point for understanding soil remediation techniques and heavy metal behavior in degraded agricultural environments.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-002</data>
