<node id="Fig. 3">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 3</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 3 refers to a figure label utilized across multiple distinct scientific contexts, each presenting unique data visualizations and analytical results. In soil chemistry research concerning phosphogypsum application, Fig. 3 illustrates the activity of macro-ions and hydroxyl ions (OH⁻) within the soil solution following treatment. These visualizations specifically present calculation outcomes generated by the ION-3 model, detailing the dynamic shifts in ion concentrations in the soil solution post-application.

In a separate study focusing on volumetric tracking, Fig. 3 functions as a data visualization that displays typical percentage curves representing the cumulative volume of phosphogypsum (PG). This representation maps volumetric accumulation or distribution trends over a specified timeframe or process stage.

Regarding material characterization, another instance of Fig. 3 presents comprehensive physical and structural data. This includes X-ray diffraction patterns alongside quantitative measurements of density, porosity, linear shrinkage, and water absorption, offering a detailed profile of the material's compositional and physical properties.

In microbiological and composting analyses, Fig. 3 is employed to display microbial diversity metrics, overall community composition, and species overlap across different composting samples. This visualization supports the evaluation of ecological dynamics and microbial community shifts throughout various composting conditions.

Finally, within environmental impact assessments, Fig. 3 illustrates the proportional contribution of each individual process and material flow to the overall environmental impacts associated with different technologies. This breakdown facilitates a comparative analysis of how specific operational steps and material inputs influence the ecological footprint of each technological pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791208777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
