<node id="Soil">
  <data key="d0">Soil</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Soil is a fundamental natural, terrestrial, and geological substrate that functions as a dynamic physical and biological matrix and a critical environmental compartment. Serving as the primary foundation for agricultural and ecological systems, it facilitates chemical mixing, root growth, microbial activity, nutrient cycling, and plant development. Due to its complex physicochemical properties, soil is extensively utilized as a natural reference medium for comparative trace element analysis, chemical concentration baselines, and scientific evaluations of heavy metal accumulation and broader ecological functions.

As a geological material, soil contains typical uranium concentrations and radionuclide activity levels that vary according to parent material composition. It is the largest source of background environmental radon, characterized by a baseline emanation fraction of 20% and typical exhalation rates measured per gram. Furthermore, the concentration of Radium-226 within soil directly determines its suitability for agricultural cultivation and residential applications.

Soil is highly vulnerable to environmental contamination and readily accumulates fluorides and potentially toxic elements from atmospheric deposition and industrial activities. It frequently receives phosphogypsum applications via stack deposition, which can leach toxic gases and polluted water into the ground. This accumulation often triggers soil acidification, altered chemical balance, reduced organic matter, and compromised structural integrity. Consequently, batch incubation studies are routinely conducted with phosphogypsum to monitor shifts in element speciation and pH. As an environmental compartment, soil also serves as a medium for plant uptake and can facilitate leaching into groundwater systems.

Given its critical role, soil is a primary focus for pollution research and agricultural management, acting as the designated site for targeted environmental interventions. Passivation and remediation technologies are deployed within soil matrices to immobilize and mitigate accumulated contaminants. Conversely, agricultural amendments such as biofertilizers and straw are applied to actively enhance porosity, density, structural stability, fertility, and nutrient availability. These interventions boost biological activity and support sustainable plant growth. Ultimately, soil operates as a complex environmental medium where ecological health, agricultural productivity, and pollution control intersect.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032</data>
