<node id="Florida">
  <data key="d0">Florida</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Florida is a U.S. state and geographic region in the United States that serves as a major hub for phosphate rock mining and processing, particularly for wet-process phosphoric acid production. The state is a primary source of phosphogypsum, a byproduct of phosphate processing that is frequently stored in large stacks and ponds. Environmental and industrial assessments in Florida have extensively documented these phosphogypsum sites, noting the presence of contaminated material, the formation of monoclinic crystals, and operational phosphate plant stacks that exhibit varying Radon-222 flux rates across different surfaces.

Scientific research in Florida has heavily focused on the radiological and chemical properties of local phosphate materials and phosphogypsum. Phosphate rocks and associated samples from the region have been routinely analyzed for uranium-238 and radium-226 activities, with the state frequently referenced in datasets for radioactive isotope measurements. Investigations have also revealed that Polonium-210 is abundant in groundwater aquifers located beneath mined lands. Consequently, Florida has been the subject of numerous studies addressing phosphogypsum disposal, soil amendments, and environmental management, including the hosting of specialized symposia dedicated to phosphogypsum research and policy.&lt;SEP&gt;Florida is a U.S. state where phosphate mining materials are processed to extract rare earth elements using chelating polymers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-013</data>
