<node id="Sodium">
  <data key="d0">Sodium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sodium is a chemical element and ion that exhibits distinct behaviors across various scientific and environmental contexts. In experimental settings, sodium ion concentration levels are frequently monitored across multiple stages, where data indicates that its levels remain highly stable, consistently tracking near the 100 mark throughout the duration of the studies.

Within the composition of phosphogypsum, sodium functions as a major element, though it is present in relatively smaller amounts compared to other primary constituents. Measured mass fractions for sodium in phosphogypsum samples typically range from 0.300% to 1.210%, a composition that aligns with standard phosphogypsum profiles. From a mineralogical perspective, sodium plays a structural role by substituting for calcium within apatite crystals, a substitution process that is essential for maintaining electrical neutrality in the mineral lattice.

In agricultural and soil science applications, sodium acts as a highly hydrated cation that accumulates on the exchange complex of sodic soils. High concentrations of this cation are known to induce clay dispersion, which can degrade soil structure. However, when phosphogypsum is applied to these soils, calcium effectively displaces the excess sodium, mitigating its adverse effects and demonstrating a practical interaction between the element and soil remediation techniques.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791187375</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
