<node id="Hydrochloric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Hydrochloric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrochloric acid is a strong mineral acid utilized across analytical and industrial chemical processes. In laboratory settings, it is frequently prepared as a 0.01 M solution specifically for the titration of carbonate and bicarbonate anions. Beyond analytical chemistry, the compound functions as a potent chemical reagent in hydrometallurgical extraction methods.

A primary application of hydrochloric acid involves the acid leaching of rare earth elements from phosphogypsum. Numerous studies characterize it as an optimal leachant that effectively dissolves the gypsum matrix, with comparative research consistently identifying it as superior to sulfuric acid for rare earth element recovery due to its strong acidic performance. However, conflicting findings exist regarding its long-term operational viability. While the majority of investigations highlight its effectiveness and superiority for extraction, other evaluations have tested it for cyclic leaching processes and concluded that it is infeasible for sustained rare earth element recovery from phosphogypsum. These discrepancies indicate that its practical success in phosphogypsum leaching likely depends on specific experimental conditions, process parameters, and whether single-pass or cyclic operations are employed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791039586</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
