<node id="Calcium-Carbonate Equilibrium">
  <data key="d0">Calcium-Carbonate Equilibrium</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium-carbonate equilibrium is a chemical process accounted for when calculating ion forms in soil solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium-carbonate equilibrium is a chemical phenomenon in soil solution that influences the molar fraction of active cadmium ions.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium-carbonate equilibrium is a chemical process accounted for when calculating ion forms in soil solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium-carbonate equilibrium is a chemical phenomenon in soil solution that influences the molar fraction of active cadmium ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-000</data>
