<node id="TENORM">
  <data key="d0">TENORM</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">TENORM is a classification for phosphogypsum indicating it contains technologically enhanced naturally occurring radioactive material.&lt;SEP&gt;TENORM refers to technologically enhanced naturally occurring radioactive materials, whose environmental limitations are re-evaluated by the Biogeosystem Technique.&lt;SEP&gt;TENORM is a classification for phosphogypsum indicating it contains technologically enhanced naturally occurring radioactive material.&lt;SEP&gt;TENORM refers to technologically enhanced naturally occurring radioactive materials, whose environmental limitations are re-evaluated by the Biogeosystem Technique.&lt;SEP&gt;TENORM refers to technologically enhanced naturally occurring radioactive materials, studied alongside NORM for uranium, thorium, potassium, and radon levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-009</data>
