<node id="South Africa">
  <data key="d0">South Africa</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">South Africa is a country hosting the Phalaborwa phosphate rock deposit.&lt;SEP&gt;South Africa is a country hosting the Phalaborwa phosphate rock deposit.&lt;SEP&gt;South Africa developed methods for co-producing sulfuric acid and cement using PG.&lt;SEP&gt;South Africa is a country whose phosphogypsum samples are investigated for cement set retardation properties.&lt;SEP&gt;South Africa is a geographic location representing a source of phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;South Africa is a country identified as a source of phosphogypsum in referenced literature.&lt;SEP&gt;South Africa is a geographic region where phosphogypsum was found to contain significantly higher levels of certain trace elements compared to other locations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008</data>
