<node id="Nickel">
  <data key="d0">Nickel</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Nickel is a chemical element classified as both a transition metal and a heavy metal, frequently examined across environmental, geological, and industrial domains. In ecological research, it is routinely studied alongside cadmium and lead due to its phytotoxicity and extraction potential. Geologically, nickel is characteristically depleted in phosphorites relative to average crustal abundances and is often found in association with organic matter.

Within industrial byproducts, nickel is a prominent trace element in phosphogypsum, where it is systematically analyzed and documented with mass concentrations recorded in micrograms per gram. As a heavy metal present in this material, it poses significant environmental and public health risks, although its mobility in seepage waters is generally curtailed by natural buffering processes. Concurrently, nickel serves a functional role in chemical engineering; when combined with phosphogypsum or iron, it acts as a key component in compound oxygen carriers designed to reduce reaction temperatures.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791187056</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lead">
  <data key="d0">Lead</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Lead is a heavy metal element that is frequently studied alongside cadmium and nickel, particularly regarding its phytotoxicity and extraction potential. It is notably present as a trace element in phosphogypsum, where its mass content significantly exceeds the Earth's crust average. Analytical measurements of phosphogypsum samples have recorded lead concentrations ranging from 4.70 to 204.29 μg/g, highlighting its substantial accumulation in this industrial byproduct.

As a heavy metal ion, lead can be released from phosphogypsum and subsequently migrate through various environmental compartments. Once dispersed, it is readily absorbed by plants from contaminated soil, which introduces significant food safety risks. Due to its persistence and toxicity, lead poses considerable environmental and health hazards. Consequently, it is subject to strict regulatory limits in water quality standards to mitigate exposure and protect both ecological and human health.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead is a trace element enriched in phosphorites, known to substitute for calcium in the apatite crystal structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead is a chemical element analyzed in phosphogypsum samples with documented concentration data.&lt;SEP&gt;Lead is a chemical element whose +2 state usually dominates and whose solubility is controlled by compounds like lead carbonate and PbSO4 in oxidizing environments.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element with a specified limit of 0.05 mg l⁻¹ across multiple regulatory frameworks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016</data>
