<node id="Surface Runoff">
  <data key="d0">Surface Runoff</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface runoff is a water flow pathway polluted by open sludge ponds from the chemical plant.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a water flow pathway polluted by open sludge ponds from the chemical plant.&lt;SEP&gt;A pathway through which high phosphorus concentration leachates are discharged into the Yangchang River.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a hydrological process that transports heavy metal complexes from land to surface water and the ocean.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface runoff is a concern related to phosphogypsum storage sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018</data>
