<node id="Ground Water">
  <data key="d0">Ground Water</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Ground water is an underground water resource polluted by open sludge ponds from the chemical plant.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground water is an underground water resource polluted by open sludge ponds from the chemical plant.&lt;SEP&gt;Ground Water is an aquifer system studied for natural radioisotopes and barium contamination.&lt;SEP&gt;An environmental medium into which uranium-thorium series radioisotopes are transported from solid materials.&lt;SEP&gt;The Ground Water is an environmental compartment receiving leaching and seepage, providing potable water to humans.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-ce9090f230bcd0bfeefe92db7a576442-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-983b2c3f393a1de00521565a70363819-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-042&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045</data>
