<node id="Phosphate Rock">
  <data key="d0">Phosphate Rock</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphate rock is a naturally occurring geological mineral resource and ore that serves as the foundational feedstock for industrial chemical production, particularly in the manufacturing of phosphoric acid and phosphate fertilizers. Geologically, it manifests as sedimentary, igneous, or metamorphic deposits and is widely distributed globally, with significant reserves found in regions such as China. The material functions as the primary raw material in wet processing and acidulation operations, where it is decomposed using concentrated sulfuric acid to solubilize its constituent elements and yield phosphoric acid.

During this chemical processing, the inherent composition of phosphate rock directly dictates the characteristics of the resulting byproducts and emissions. The fluorine content naturally present in the rock reacts to form hydrogen fluoride, while uranium partitions into the phosphoric acid stream and certain radium-226 particles may survive the treatment. The geological makeup of the ore also introduces impurities, such as aluminum and titanium-bearing particles, into the phosphogypsum matrix, a major solid byproduct of the process. Industrial operations frequently manage this waste stream by recovering residual sulfuric acid from phosphogypsum leaching cycles for reuse in mineral treatment.

Beyond its role in agriculture and chemical manufacturing, phosphate rock is intrinsically linked to significant radiological and critical mineral attributes. It inherently contains naturally occurring radioactive materials, including uranium, thorium, and radium isotopes maintained in radioactive equilibrium. This distinct radiological profile not only characterizes the rock alongside its phosphogypsum byproduct but also establishes it as a standard comparative baseline in radionuclide analysis. Furthermore, the ore acts as a valuable secondary geological source of rare earth elements and lanthanides, which occur as natural impurities. The concentration of these critical minerals varies by geological origin and is typically recovered through hydrometallurgical extraction processes, with some elements persisting in the phosphogypsum waste. Ultimately, phosphate rock represents a complex geological resource that bridges primary extraction, chemical processing, and secondary critical mineral recovery, while remaining closely tied to its associated waste profiles and radiological considerations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005</data>
