  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Environmental impact assessment focuses on the proximity of industrial sites to the Black Sea and associated risks.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental impact refers to the ecological consequences of phosphogypsum management and utilization, a key theme in the literature.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental impact represents the ecological consequences of Phosphogypsum production and disposal, a key focus of the study.&lt;SEP&gt;A broad category encompassing damage indicators such as eutrophication, acidification, and global warming.&lt;SEP&gt;Environmental Impact is the aggregate ecological consequence measured across multiple indicators from Phosphogypsum disposal.</data>
