<node id="CaO">
  <data key="d0">CaO</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium oxide is a major chemical constituent in cement clinker, granulated slag, and phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;CaO is an alkaline substance used in base-washing procedures to adjust the pH of the PG system.&lt;SEP&gt;CaO is a chemical compound mentioned as a potential constituent measured in phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;CaO is a product formed from the oxidation of CaS and the decomposition of PG.&lt;SEP&gt;CaO is a compound compared thermodynamically during PG decomposition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-011</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791090248</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
