  <data key="d2">Calcium fluoride is a specific fluoride compound tested for solubility.&lt;SEP&gt;CaF2 is a chemical compound present in CWBS and PG that crystallizes at 700 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;CaF2 is a solid-phase compound containing fluorine that exists at temperatures between 100 and 400 °C.&lt;SEP&gt;CaF2 (calcium fluoride) is a precipitate formed when calcium carbonate removes fluoride.</data>
