<node id="Portland Slag Cement">
  <data key="d0">Portland Slag Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Portland slag cement is a building material whose manufacture can utilize purified phosphogypsum as a raw material.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland slag cement is a construction material whose properties are similarly affected by the addition of phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland slag cement is a construction material produced by intergrinding granulated slag, cement clinker, and gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland Slag Cement is a cement type whose autoclave expansion and heat of hydration comply with standard requirements when using purified phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Portland slag cement is a binding material whose physical properties are modified by the addition of thermally treated phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791023151</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aqueous Citric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Aqueous Citric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aqueous citric acid is a solution used to measure solubility and purify phosphogypsum by reacting with impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Aqueous Citric Acid is a chemical solution used to treat phosphogypsum for purification by removing impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Aqueous citric acid is the specific form of citric acid used to treat phosphogypsum samples, with optimal concentrations varying by sample type.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004</data>
