<node id="Compressive Strength">
  <data key="d0">Compressive Strength</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Compressive strength is a fundamental mechanical and physical property that indicates a material's load-bearing capacity, typically measured in megapascals (MPa). It is commonly evaluated using a universal testing machine on cylindrical samples and demonstrates a linear relationship with density. For cement and plaster applications, this property is routinely assessed at 1, 3, 7, and 28 days.

In construction materials, including cemented paste backfill (CPB) mixtures, alternative binders, and phosphogypsum-based mixtures, compressive strength serves as a critical performance metric. Its behavior varies significantly based on composition and treatment: while higher fractions of phosphogypsum generally reduce compressive strength compared to natural gypsum, utilizing purified phosphogypsum can actually increase it in gypsum plaster. Additionally, optimal thermal pretreatment enhances the compressive strength of CPB mixtures.

In the specific context of composite bone cement, compressive strength increases with longer incubation times but experiences a slight decrease as the concentration of sodium chloride (NaCl) additives rises. Overall, compressive strength serves as a vital indicator of structural integrity across diverse engineering and biomedical applications, heavily influenced by material formulation, processing methods, and environmental conditioning.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791060756</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Setting Time">
  <data key="d0">Setting Time</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Setting Time is a fundamental physical property and measured parameter that quantifies the duration required for various cementitious and plaster materials to harden. It is typically recorded in two distinct phases: the initial and final hardening stages. As a critical characteristic, it directly influences the handling properties of the material and is optimized differently depending on the intended application, such as dental versus orthopedic uses. The property is evaluated across several material types, including general cement, cement paste, gypsum plaster, and composite bone cement.

The setting time exhibits distinct behaviors and sensitivities depending on the specific material composition and additives. In general cement and cement paste, the presence of phosphogypsum considerably retards the setting time, a phenomenon attributed to the formation of protective coatings on the material. Conversely, when gypsum plaster is manufactured from purified phosphogypsum, its setting time actually increases. In the context of bone cement and composite bone cement, the setting time decreases as the concentration of sodium chloride increases. These variations highlight how chemical additives and base material purity directly modulate the hardening duration, necessitating precise control to meet specific clinical or industrial handling requirements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791060479</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
