<node id="Bulk Density">
  <data key="d0">Bulk Density</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Bulk density is a physical property representing the mass per unit volume of gypsum plaster samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk Density is a physical property of gypsum plaster that increases when produced from purified phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk density is a physical property of phosphogypsum, typically ranging from 1.40 to 1.85 g/cm³.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk density is a physical property modelled across soil organic matter and land-use continua.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical measurement of phosphogypsum stacks ranging between 0.9 and 1.7 g/cm3.&lt;SEP&gt;Bulk Density is a soil physical property that decreases when calcium induces flocculation of soil particles.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-030&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004</data>
