<node id="Solubility">
  <data key="d0">Solubility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Solubility refers to the ability of phosphatic and fluoride compounds to dissolve in water and aqueous citric acid solutions.&lt;SEP&gt;Solubility is the measured property indicating the amount of substance dissolved per 100ml of citric acid solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Solubility is the measured property indicating how much of a calcium phosphate compound dissolves in the aqueous citric acid solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Solubility is a chemical property that determines the concentration of elements in solution, heavily influenced by pH, redox conditions, and compound formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Solubility is the capacity of a substance to dissolve, governed by environmental factors like pH and Eh.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-017</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189670</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chemical Composition">
  <data key="d0">Chemical Composition</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Chemical composition refers to the percentage breakdown of constituents like P₂O₅, F, organic matter, and Na₂O + K₂O in the phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A material property that influences the setting duration of cement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006</data>
