<node id="Sulphuric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Sulphuric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Sulphuric acid is a chemical used in alternative treatment methods to reduce phosphates and fluorides in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Sulphuric acid is used to acidify rock phosphate to produce various fluoride and phosphate compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical reagent used in the wet process to attack phosphate rocks for phosphoric acid production.&lt;SEP&gt;A product generated by the PSC process, with a production quantity of 408.00 kg.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015</data>
