<node id="Hydrofluoric Acid">
  <data key="d0">Hydrofluoric Acid</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrofluoric acid is a highly reactive, water-soluble aqueous solution that functions as a significant chemical byproduct and industrial reagent. It is primarily generated during the wet process of phosphoric acid manufacturing, where hydrogen fluoride reacts with silicate impurities present in phosphate rock. The compound can also be produced through the reaction of fluorides with aqueous citric acid. During these formation processes, hydrofluoric acid frequently interacts with silica to yield hexafluorosilicic acid, establishing its role as a reactive chemical product within various reaction pathways.

In industrial applications, hydrofluoric acid is extensively utilized as a chemical reagent to remove quartz phases and convert specific components within phosphogypsum during processing. It also persists as a residual acid within phosphogypsum, directly contributing to the material's highly corrosive and acidic properties. Beyond its involvement in phosphate and gypsum processing, hydrofluoric acid is widely recognized for its practical use as an etching agent for glass and silicon-based materials, leveraging its strong chemical reactivity for precision manufacturing and material treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrofluoric acid is a harmful free acid present in phosphogypsum that reacts with quicklime to form inert salts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791207316</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
