<node id="Calcium Dihydrogen Phosphate Monohydrate">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Dihydrogen Phosphate Monohydrate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium dihydrogen phosphate monohydrate is a phosphatic compound that exhibits maximum solubility in aqueous citric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium dihydrogen phosphate monohydrate is a chemical compound possibly precipitated on the surface of phosphogypsum crystals.&lt;SEP&gt;A water-soluble compound potentially assigned to precipitation in the studied samples.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004</data>
