<node id="Fig. 1">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 1</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 1 illustrates the solubility of phosphates in aqueous citric acid at 30°C.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure illustrating the distribution of rare earth elements in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 1 illustrates the scheme of the radioanalytical procedure used for uranium separation and radon measurement.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure illustrating changes in compost pile temperature and water content during biofertilizer preparation.&lt;SEP&gt;A diagram illustrating the system boundaries of various phosphogypsum disposal methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791207433</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fig. 2">
  <data key="d0">Fig. 2</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Fig. 2 illustrates the solubility of fluorides in aqueous citric acid at 30°C.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 2 displays the X-ray diffraction patterns of the samples obtained from different configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Fig. 2 displays a typical alpha-spectra of uranium isotopes measured in a phosphogypsum waste sample.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure comparing the physical and chemical properties of soil amended with biofertilizer versus unamended soil.&lt;SEP&gt;A figure presenting LCA results for different PG disposal methods with various environmental impact units.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007</data>
