  <data key="d5">1790961592</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dihydrate Process">
  <data key="d0">Dihydrate Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The dihydrate process is a method for manufacturing phosphoric acid that produces phosphogypsum as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;The dihydrate process is the most common industrial method for producing phosphoric acid using calcium sulfate dihydrate.&lt;SEP&gt;The Dihydrate Process is a specific wet phosphoric acid production method that produces phosphogypsum filter cakes with notable impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hemihydrate Process">
  <data key="d0">Hemihydrate Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The hemihydrate process is a two-step method for manufacturing phosphoric acid that produces phosphogypsum as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;The hemihydrate process is a widely used industrial method that produces purer phosphoric acid with higher P2O5 concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Hemihydrate Process is a production method that yields phosphogypsum with relatively high impurities and lacks uranium extraction capability.&lt;SEP&gt;The hemihydrate process is a wet phosphoric acid method that yields higher uranium content (5-100 μg/g) due to its crystal structure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
