<node id="P2O5">
  <data key="d0">P2O5</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">P2O5 is a chemical compound representing phosphorus content that is targeted for mitigation in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 is a chemical compound representing the phosphorus pentoxide content in crude phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 is a lattice-bounded impurity within the gypsum lattice that is difficult to remove via water-washing.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 (phosphorus pentoxide) is a soluble impurity measured in the purified gypsum product.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 is a chemical metric used to measure the total production volume of phosphate fertilizer.&lt;SEP&gt;P2O5 is a compound comprising less than 1% of phosphogypsum material, yet high application rates significantly increase available soil phosphorus.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028</data>
