<node id="Wet Process">
  <data key="d0">Wet Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Wet Process is a prevalent industrial chemical manufacturing method primarily utilized for the production of phosphoric acid and phosphate fertilizers. This procedure centers on the acidulation of phosphate rock, specifically fluorapatite, using concentrated sulfuric acid. By treating the raw phosphate material with sulfuric acid, the process efficiently extracts phosphoric acid, establishing it as a foundational technique in modern phosphoric acid plants and fertilizer manufacturing facilities.

Beyond the primary acidulation reaction, the Wet Process involves several distinct chemical transformations and material variations. During the treatment of phosphate rock, hydrofluoric acid is generated and subsequently reacts with silica to form hexafluorosilicic acid. The procedure also significantly impacts the chemical composition of associated byproducts, notably determining the variation of phosphates found in phosphogypsum. Furthermore, as an industrial chemical procedure for processing phosphate rock, the Wet Process actively redistributes and fractionates U-series radionuclides throughout the material stream.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical production method whose efficiency and type affect phosphogypsum composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Wet process refers to the industrial production method used to generate phosphoric acid, influencing phosphogypsum composition.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
