<node id="WBS">
  <data key="d0">WBS</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">WBS, which stands for Washed Beneficiated Solid, is a processed residual solid matrix derived from phosphogypsum (PG) following solubilization procedures. Initially functioning as a raw material sample, it undergoes a treatment process where quartz and other mineral phases are removed. The material is subjected to a permutations protocol for residual gangue removal, and soluble sodium sulfates are systematically eliminated. Chemically, WBS primarily consists of calcium fluoride and quartz, forming a distinct solid matrix that acts as a washed beneficiated concentrate with an increased concentration of rare earth elements (REEs). These REEs are specifically enriched through coprecipitation with phosphate and fluorine.

As a specialized sample type, WBS is routinely analyzed to determine the precise concentrations of REEs and various main metal elements. The material represents a targeted byproduct or solution phase where valuable components are concentrated, making it a critical subject for elemental assessment and recovery optimization. Its comprehensive processing ensures that gangue materials are minimized while preserving the enriched metallic and rare earth fractions for further evaluation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983599</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
