<node id="EDTA">
  <data key="d0">EDTA</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical compound used to assess metal complexation and facilitate the elimination of gypsum compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;A pH-dependent chelating agent used in alkaline and acidic treatments to solubilize gypsum and concentrate rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical component analyzed via mass spectrometry alongside Calcium Sulfate Dihydrate.&lt;SEP&gt;A chelating agent that binds with Praseodymium to form the [EDTA-Pr]⁻ complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-014</data>
