<node id="TWBS">
  <data key="d0">TWBS</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">TWBS is a processed sample derived from PG, analyzed using X-ray diffraction.&lt;SEP&gt;The treated version of WBS, containing transformed compounds like sodium fluorosilicates.&lt;SEP&gt;TWBS is a sample type analyzed for the concentration of REEs and main metal elements.&lt;SEP&gt;TWBS is a thermally treated beneficiated concentrate with the highest rare earth element enrichment.&lt;SEP&gt;TWBS is a final beneficiated concentrate produced after hydrofluoric acid treatment of WBS, characterized by high calcium fluoride and sodium fluorosilicate content.&lt;SEP&gt;Process associated with a 94.57 percent concentration and total enrichment of Rare Earth Elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983741</data>
