<node id="Life Cycle Assessment">
  <data key="d0">Life Cycle Assessment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Life Cycle Assessment is a systematic and comprehensive analytical framework and methodology designed to evaluate the environmental performance, impacts, resource consumption, and emissions associated with various products, processes, industrial operations, and waste management strategies. As a standardized analytical procedure, it provides a structured approach to quantifying ecological footprints and assessing environmental challenges across diverse technological and material applications.

In practical applications, Life Cycle Assessment has been utilized to evaluate the environmental impacts of recovering rare earth elements from waste fluorescent powders. It is also employed to analyze the environmental and economic challenges, performance, and sensitivity of different phosphogypsum utilization technologies. Additionally, the methodology serves as a comparative tool for assessing the environmental impacts of various disposal and utilization methods for Plaster of Paris (PG). Through these diverse implementations, Life Cycle Assessment functions as a versatile instrument for measuring resource efficiency and ecological impacts, supporting sustainable decision-making in industrial and waste management contexts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791207824</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
