<node id="Rare Earth Elements (REEs)">
  <data key="d0">Rare Earth Elements (REEs)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A group of chemical elements whose concentrations in samples PG1 and PG2 are quantified in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Rare earth elements are a group of metals including yttrium, lanthanum, cerium, and neodymium that are dispersed on phosphogypsum surfaces and concentrate during processing.&lt;SEP&gt;A group of chemical elements that occur in nature and are the primary focus of the study regarding their occurrence, speciation, and recovery.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Na4EDTA">
  <data key="d0">Na4EDTA</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Na4EDTA is a chemical agent used to solubilize the majority of phosphogypsum mass under alkaline conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Solubilization">
  <data key="d0">Solubilization</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Solubilization refers to the chemical process of dissolving quartz from the washed solid using hydrofluoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;The chemical process by which compounds like CSD and SiO2 dissolve into solutions, influenced by pH and concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Solubilization is a chemical process used to dissolve specific phases of phosphogypsum and WBS to enrich rare earth element concentrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrofluoric Acid (HF)">
  <data key="d0">Hydrofluoric Acid (HF)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical reagent used to solubilize quartz from WBS in the hydrometallurgical treatment approach.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical agent used to dissolve SiO2 through a heterogeneous reaction mechanism.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrofluoric acid is a chemical agent used to solubilize WBS, removing silicon dioxide and transforming metal compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Hydrofluoric acid is a chemical byproduct of the acidulation process that remains in PG due to industrial separation limitations.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791023270</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Lattice Bound REEs">
  <data key="d0">Lattice Bound REEs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Lattice bound REEs represent a mode of rare earth element occurrence where metals are structurally incorporated within gypsum crystal lattices.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isomorphism Substitution">
  <data key="d0">Isomorphism Substitution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Isomorphism substitution represents a mode of rare earth element occurrence where metals replace other ions within a mineral structure.&lt;SEP&gt;A process where REEs are incorporated into the calcium sulfate lattice via heterovalent replacement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-013</data>
