<node id="Washed Solid (WBS)">
  <data key="d0">Washed Solid (WBS)</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A processed solid material obtained after washing the initial BS with distilled water and subsequent drying, homogenizing, grinding, and sieving.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Centrifugation">
  <data key="d0">Centrifugation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Centrifugation is a separation technique used to isolate the liquid phase from the residual insoluble solid phase.&lt;SEP&gt;A separation technique applied for 15 minutes at 3000 rpm to process the initial material before washing.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quartz (SiO2)">
  <data key="d0">Quartz (SiO2)</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">The substantial component of WBS targeted for solubilization using hydrofluoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;A mineral phase present in WBS that undergoes removal and transformation during the hydrometallurgical process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vacuum Filtration">
  <data key="d0">Vacuum Filtration</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A separation technique used to isolate the solid phase (TWBS) from the liquid filtrate after acid treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Treated Solid (TWBS)">
  <data key="d0">Treated Solid (TWBS)</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">The solid phase remaining after vacuum filtration, which is dried, homogenized, ground, sieved, and stored for analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PG1">
  <data key="d0">PG1</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A sample material analyzed for the concentration of rare earth elements and main metal elements.&lt;SEP&gt;PG1 is the source sample from which WBS and TWBS were obtained for elemental analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PG2">
  <data key="d0">PG2</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">A sample material analyzed for the concentration of rare earth elements and main metal elements.&lt;SEP&gt;PG2 is the specific source material from which BS, WBS, and CWBS samples were obtained.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Concentration">
  <data key="d0">Concentration</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A quantitative metric measured in parts per million (ppm) to determine the abundance of REEs and metal elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Concentration quantifies the amount of elements in samples, measured in parts per million (ppm).&lt;SEP&gt;A key hydrometallurgical parameter influencing the removal of quartz and solubilization of compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;A variable in the mathematical formula likely representing the concentration of a titrant or standard solution.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-018</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791141567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Magnetic Agitation Speed">
  <data key="d0">Magnetic Agitation Speed</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A controlled hydrometallurgical parameter during the agitation of hydrofluoric acid and WBS.&lt;SEP&gt;A key hydrometallurgical parameter affecting the efficiency of the quartz removal process.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Contact Time">
  <data key="d0">Contact Time</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A controlled hydrometallurgical parameter representing the duration of interaction between hydrofluoric acid and WBS.&lt;SEP&gt;A key hydrometallurgical parameter that influences the duration and effectiveness of the treatment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1790983967</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Pyrometallurgical Approach">
  <data key="d0">Pyrometallurgical Approach</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Pyrometallurgical Approach is a thermal treatment method analogous to rare earth ores enrichment, involving calcination.&lt;SEP&gt;A thermal processing method analogous to rare earth element ore enrichment, referenced in the calcination step.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-002</data>
