<node id="Silicon">
  <data key="d0">Silicon</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Silicon is a chemical element whose concentration was determined using Atomic Absorption Spectroscopy.&lt;SEP&gt;An element liberated from quartz after breaking siloxane covalent bonds.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon is an elemental component of dried PG, comprising 0.56 wt%.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element concentrated in specific spots, indicating silica impurities or silicate inclusions.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon is a component in PG that improves the anti-agglomeration capability of the oxygen carrier.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon is an impurity in phosphogypsum that improves sintering resistance when used as an oxygen carrier.&lt;SEP&gt;A major element present in phosphogypsum samples, with measured mass fractions ranging from 8.640% to 31.000%.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004</data>
