  <data key="d0">Scanning Electron Microscopy</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A microscopy technique used to analyze sample morphology and map rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Scanning Electron Microscopy is an analytical technique used to examine the surface morphology and elemental distribution of raw and leached phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Scanning electron microscopy is an imaging modality used to analyze the microscopic morphology and surface texture of phosphogypsum particles.&lt;SEP&gt;A microscopy technique used to generate high-magnification micrographs and technical metadata.&lt;SEP&gt;Scanning Electron Microscopy is an imaging technique used to examine the microstructure of phosphogypsum.</data>
