  <data key="d2">Europium is a chemical element whose concentration and enrichment were measured in the samples.&lt;SEP&gt;A critical rare earth element categorized by Seredin, found in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Europium is a rare earth element measured in WBS and TWBS samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Europium is a rare earth element whose stability in calcium sulfate was investigated.&lt;SEP&gt;Europium is a critical rare earth element present in a considerable proportion in dried PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Europium is a rare earth element analyzed in Idaho phosphogypsum with a mean concentration of 1.2 mg/kg.</data>
