  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A chemical element used as a dopant with Erbium to facilitate calcium fluoride crystallization at lower temperatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Ytterbium is a rare earth element measured in WBS and TWBS samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Ytterbium is a rare earth element with a concentration below the detection limit in the analyzed sample.&lt;SEP&gt;Ytterbium is a rare earth element enriched in phosphorites relative to shale.&lt;SEP&gt;Ytterbium is a rare earth element analyzed in Idaho phosphogypsum with a mean concentration of 2.8 mg/kg.</data>
