  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A phase transition process whose temperature threshold for calcium fluoride was reduced by doping with Erbium and Ytterbium.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallization is a thermal process occurring between 600 °C and 700 °C that explains phase changes in CaF2.&lt;SEP&gt;Crystallization is a process used to capture carbon dioxide and produce calcium carbonate while removing soluble impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015</data>
