<node id="900 °C">
  <data key="d0">900 °C</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">900 °C is the temperature at which calcium fluoride crystallization typically occurs according to Dash et al.&lt;SEP&gt;A temperature at which F exists as solid-phase CaSiFO and gas-phase HF.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-26bca3d4f742299ce2dbcd6381558f89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-007</data>
