<node id="Wet Processing">
  <data key="d0">Wet Processing</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Wet Processing is the industrial technique used to produce phosphoric acid from phosphate rock, generating PG waste as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Wet processing is the industrial procedure used to treat phosphate rock, which leads to the formation of phosphogypsum waste.&lt;SEP&gt;Wet processing is the industrial method used to produce phosphoric acid from phosphate rock, generating phosphogypsum waste.</data>
