<node id="Potassium">
  <data key="d0">Potassium</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Potassium is a natural radionuclide whose concentration ($C_{\text{K}}$) is used in the Ra-Eq calculation.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium is a primary chemical component of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A major element present in phosphogypsum samples, with measured mass fractions ranging from 0.040% to 1.200%.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium content is measured using the classical sodium tetraphenylboron method.&lt;SEP&gt;A soil nutrient parameter increased by microbial activity during fermentation and humification.&lt;SEP&gt;Potassium is an essential plant nutrient uptake enhanced by the interaction between biofertilizers and microorganisms.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013</data>
