  <data key="d3">doc-80bac46661a7d25358c897f5feccea99-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d2">Rn-220 is comparable to Rn-222 as a short-lived radon gas.&lt;SEP&gt;A radon gas that may diffuse out of phosphate rock, reducing the activity of subsequent radionuclides in the decay series.&lt;SEP&gt;Radon-222 is a radioactive noble gas produced by the alpha decay of Ra-226, known for its high mobility and environmental significance.&lt;SEP&gt;A radon isotope that escapes from solid phases and decays from Ra-226, with a 3.82-day half-life.&lt;SEP&gt;Rn-222 is the specific radioactive isotope of radon gas that is the primary focus of exposure studies.</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791183363</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
