<node id="Ordinary Portland Cement">
  <data key="d0">Ordinary Portland Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Ordinary Portland Cement is a conventional binder material whose large-scale demand contributes to significant carbon emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;The most conventional binder used in phosphogypsum remediation and CPB mixtures to balance structural safety and sustainability.&lt;SEP&gt;Ordinary Portland Cement is a primary cementitious constituent in CPB mixtures whose proportion affects mechanical performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Ordinary Portland Cement is a conventional binder whose production generates substantial greenhouse gas emissions.&lt;SEP&gt;Ordinary Portland Cement is a conventional binder produced from limestone and clay, serving as a baseline for alternative binder comparisons.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
