<node id="Fluorapatite">
  <data key="d0">Fluorapatite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fluorapatite is a calcium phosphate fluoride mineral characterized by anion substitution with other phosphates. Chemically, it serves as the primary compound in which fluoride precipitates, particularly within CPB mixtures. In geological and industrial settings, it is commonly found in phosphogypsum, where it actively contributes to fluorine leaching. As a mineral form of calcium phosphate, Fluorapatite functions as the principal raw material and reactant in the wet process, operating as the primary acidified phosphate ore.

During industrial processing, Fluorapatite drives the formation of fertilizers and gypsum while simultaneously generating potentially toxic elements as byproducts. Furthermore, within specific operational and geological systems, it acts as the exclusive reservoir for critical materials, serving as the sole source that contains 100% of the target rare earth elements. This dual role as both a foundational phosphate reactant and a concentrated rare earth deposit underscores its multifaceted significance in chemical manufacturing and resource extraction.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorapatite is the specific chemical form of apatite found in igneous rocks, with the formula Ca5(PO4)3F.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorapatite is a mineral that can contain up to 1% rare earth elements by mass and may control fluorine solubility in phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791186193</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
