  <data key="d2">Wastewater is produced in substantial volumes by the water-washing method, requiring secondary treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Wastewater is a byproduct of leaching processes that poses environmental challenges due to high volume and acid content.&lt;SEP&gt;Wastewater is a byproduct of the leaching process, specifically acidic calcium sulfate-saturated water that needs to be minimized.&lt;SEP&gt;A byproduct of all three processes that is 100% reused.</data>
