  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium aluminate cement is an alternative binder that provides aluminate for ettringite formation in CPB systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium Aluminate Cement is manufactured using limestone and bauxite, offering low CO emissions and high early mechanical properties as an alternative binder.&lt;SEP&gt;A cement type used in backfill applications for fluorides immobilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium aluminate cement is a specific type of cement listed as an application for phosphogypsum in the cement industry.&lt;SEP&gt;A construction material whose hydration properties and strength are affected by phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-023</data>
