<node id="Atmosphere">
  <data key="d0">Atmosphere</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Atmosphere is the environmental medium where fluorine moves via adsorption and volatilization.&lt;SEP&gt;The atmospheric environment where phosphogypsum emissions, chemical reactions, and pollutant retention occur.&lt;SEP&gt;The atmosphere is an environmental compartment where phosphogypsum particles and heavy metals migrate via airflow and precipitation.&lt;SEP&gt;The external environment where Rn-222 gas reaches after diffusing through pore spaces.&lt;SEP&gt;The Atmosphere is an environmental compartment receiving emissions such as radon-222, fluoride gas, and dust from the gypsum stack.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-017&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045</data>
