<node id="Q.S. Chen">
  <data key="d0">Q.S. Chen</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Q.S. Chen is a researcher whose academic work centers on the environmental remediation and geotechnical application of industrial byproducts, with a primary emphasis on phosphogypsum and cemented paste backfill systems. Their research portfolio includes multiple studies dedicated to understanding the retention, immobilization, and leaching behaviors of phosphorus and fluorides within these backfill matrices. Notably, Chen has co-authored and authored publications that document the effective capture of phosphorus and fluorine in phosphogypsum-based backfill, with key findings disseminated in the journal Environ. Res. The researcher has also investigated the solidification of phosphogypsum and evaluated the leaching characteristics of fluoride to ensure long-term environmental safety in backfill applications.

In addition to foundational phosphogypsum studies, Q.S. Chen has explored advanced material synergies and alternative additives to enhance contaminant retention. This includes research on highly efficient fluoride retention achieved by synergizing cemented paste backfill with poly-aluminum chloride, as well as the immobilization of fluorides using calcium aluminate cement backfill. The researcher’s scope also extends to addressing phosphate uptake constraints and assessing the viability of modified copper slag for backfill utilization. Collectively, these contributions underscore a consistent focus on optimizing backfill formulations, immobilizing hazardous elements, and advancing the sustainable engineering use of phosphogypsum and supplementary industrial materials.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-022&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-015</data>
