<node id="Phosphate Ores">
  <data key="d0">Phosphate Ores</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphate Ores are raw mineral resources excavated for modern agriculture and fertilizer production.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate ores are raw geological materials from which phosphogypsum is derived, containing varying gangue minerals and fluoride content.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate ores are the raw materials excavated worldwide, with data tracked by the USGS database.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate ores are the raw materials processed in the phosphoric acid industry, containing trace amounts of rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate ores are mineral deposits characterized by high natural radioactivity and trace element enrichment.</data>
