  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Biochar is an agricultural supplement added to phosphogypsum to prevent element transfer to the food chain.&lt;SEP&gt;Biochar is a carbon-rich material used as a soil amendment to attenuate toxic elements and improve soil properties.&lt;SEP&gt;A green additive used in cement-based composites, often combined with carbon dioxide curing.&lt;SEP&gt;Biochar is a material produced from gypsum pond wastewater augmented with potassium, phosphorus, and sulfur to mitigate toxic elements.</data>
