<node id="Eutrophication">
  <data key="d0">Eutrophication</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">An environmental condition primarily caused by phosphate export from soil to water bodies, leading to nutrient overload.&lt;SEP&gt;Eutrophication is an ecological consequence triggered by excess phosphate loads from phosphogypsum entering natural water bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;A condition caused by phosphorus enrichment that alters the survival environment of phytoplankton and affects biodiversity.&lt;SEP&gt;Eutrophication is an ecological process in waterways that may be enhanced by phosphorus runoff from phosphogypsum-treated agricultural sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-033</data>
