<node id="Iron">
  <data key="d0">Iron</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Iron is a chemical element and transition metal that exhibits diverse roles across environmental science, industrial processing, and materials engineering. In agricultural and soil chemistry contexts, iron actively binds with phosphate, precipitating it into insoluble forms. This fixation mechanism substantially reduces the bioavailability and plant availability of phosphate, directly influencing soil nutrient dynamics.

Within the processing of phosphogypsum (PG), iron serves as both a compositional component and a processing challenge. It constitutes approximately 0.31 wt% of dried PG and functions as a co-leached impurity during extraction procedures. The efficiency of iron co-leaching increases under conditions of prolonged processing time or elevated temperatures. Furthermore, the presence of this impurity complicates downstream purification efforts, particularly in the separation and recovery of rare earth elements from PG streams.

In advanced materials science, iron is strategically utilized to develop compound oxygen carriers for sustainable applications. As a transition metal, it can be combined with phosphogypsum or integrated with nickel to synthesize these specialized carriers. These iron-based compounds are engineered to lower reaction temperatures during chemical transformations, making them highly valuable for clean energy development and efficient industrial processes.&lt;SEP&gt;A trace element present in phosphogypsum samples, with measured mass contents ranging from 10.7 to 30.00 μg/g.&lt;SEP&gt;Iron is a chemical element listed in the water quality standards table with specified concentration limits.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element with a limit of 0.3 mg l⁻¹ and a WHO guideline value of 300 mg l⁻¹.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188835</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
