<node id="Density">
  <data key="d0">Density</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">A physical property of construction materials that is reduced by phosphogypsum incorporation.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property of the cement paste measured in grams per cubic centimeter.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical property of the composite bone cement that slightly decreases with increasing sodium chloride content.&lt;SEP&gt;Density ($\rho$) is a physical property that decreases slightly with higher NaCl additive concentration and has a linear relationship with compressive strength.&lt;SEP&gt;Density is a fundamental physical characteristic of phosphogypsum that affects its transportation and application methods.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-002</data>
