<node id="Leachate">
  <data key="d0">Leachate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Polluted liquid formed in stockpile sites that requires isolation barriers to prevent acidic and polluted formation.&lt;SEP&gt;Leachate is the liquid phase involved in the diffusion steps of the rare earth element extraction process from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A liquid solution containing accumulated rare earth elements generated during the cycle leaching process.&lt;SEP&gt;Percolating liquid from phosphogypsum characterized by high concentrations of total phosphorus and sulfate ions.&lt;SEP&gt;Leachate is a liquid mixture from phosphogypsum storage that contains toxic heavy metal and non-heavy metal pollutants.&lt;SEP&gt;Liquid that percolates through phosphogypsum storage, requiring study for environmental safety.&lt;SEP&gt;A substance identified as a potential source of the reddish liquid pools on the ground.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-011</data>
