  <data key="d0">Silicon Tetrafluoride</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Silicon tetrafluoride is a gaseous form of emitted fluoride that can directly enter plant leaves through cuticles or stomata.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon tetrafluoride is a chemical compound produced from silicate impurities in phosphate rock that hydrolyzes to form fluorosilicic acid.&lt;SEP&gt;Silicon tetrafluoride is a gaseous compound produced from the reaction of hydrofluoric acid with silicate impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-001</data>
