<node id="Cycle Leaching">
  <data key="d0">Cycle Leaching</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Cycle leaching is a method examined to reduce wastewater generation and enrich Rare Earth Elements in the aqueous solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Cycle leaching is a process where recycled hydrochloric acid solution is repeatedly used to leach fresh phosphogypsum to concentrate rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Cycle leaching is a repeated extraction procedure that evaluates the feasibility and efficiency of acid solutions over multiple iterations.&lt;SEP&gt;A leaching technique using recycled leachate to accumulate and enrich rare earth concentration.&lt;SEP&gt;Cycle leaching is a recovery technique based on the recrystallization of the gypsum matrix to extract rare earth elements.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791038121</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gravity Separation">
  <data key="d0">Gravity Separation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Gravity Separation is a physical separation technique used in the proposed process to concentrate rare earth elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Gravity separation is a physical separation technique suggested to recover undissolved rare earth element inclusions from phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;A physical separation process recommended based on density differences between rare earth phases and gypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Gravity separation is a physical process that isolates rare earth element mineral inclusions from the gypsum matrix based on differences in morphology and specific gravity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791038121</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Isomorphous Substitution">
  <data key="d0">Isomorphous Substitution</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Isomorphous Substitution describes the mechanism where Rare Earth Elements replace Calcium ions within the gypsum lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;Isomorphous substitution describes the chemical occurrence state where rare earth elements replace other ions within the phosphogypsum crystal lattice.&lt;SEP&gt;Isomorphous substitution is a chemical occurrence state where rare earth elements replace other elements within the crystal structure of phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791038121</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Soluble Rare Earth Elements Salts">
  <data key="d0">Soluble Rare Earth Elements Salts</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Soluble rare earth elements salts represent a chemical form of rare earth elements present in phosphogypsum that can be easily leached.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791038121</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
