  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791039701</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leaching Residue">
  <data key="d0">Leaching Residue</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Leaching Residue is the solid material remaining after leaching, analyzed to clarify the relationship between efficiency and occurrence state.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaching Residue is the solid material remaining after the leaching process, analyzed via microscopic characterization.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaching Residue is the solid material remaining after the leaching process, containing undissolved mineral inclusions and impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791039701</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gypsum Matrix">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Matrix</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum Matrix refers to the calcium sulfate dihydrate structure within Phosphogypsum that dissolves and recrystallizes during leaching.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791039701</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Gypsum Coating">
  <data key="d0">Gypsum Coating</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gypsum Coating is a layer of calcium sulfate dihydrate that can hinder the dissolution of dispersed soluble Rare Earth Element salts.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791039701</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Leaching Efficiency">
  <data key="d0">Leaching Efficiency</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Leaching Efficiency is a performance metric measured during the extraction of rare earth elements from PG.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaching Efficiency is a calculated metric representing the proportion of rare earth elements extracted from raw phosphogypsum into the leaching solution.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaching Efficiency measures the success rate of Rare Earth Element extraction under varying experimental conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaching efficiency is a key performance metric that decreases significantly with increased leaching cycles due to gypsum saturation.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaching Efficiency is a metric evaluating the effectiveness of acid extraction of Rare Earth Elements from Phosphogypsum under various conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Leaching efficiency is a quantitative metric measuring the percentage of rare earth elements successfully extracted during each leaching cycle.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791039701</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Occurrence of REEs">
  <data key="d0">Occurrence of REEs</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Occurrence of REEs describes the different physical and chemical states in which Rare Earth Elements exist within Phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791039701</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Reaction Temperature">
  <data key="d0">Reaction Temperature</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Reaction Temperature is a controlled experimental parameter, tested at 30°C and ambient temperature, affecting leaching efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;The thermal condition required to drive the CLG process, with an optimum range of 750-850 °C for PG-CuFe2O4.&lt;SEP&gt;Reaction temperature refers to the thermal conditions required for the gasification reaction to proceed efficiently.&lt;SEP&gt;Reaction temperature is a critical parameter that decreased from 910°C to 590°C for reduction and from 1100°C to 1000°C for oxidation when using a catalyst.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791089698</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Stirring Speed">
  <data key="d0">Stirring Speed</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Stirring Speed indicates the agitation rate during leaching, optimized at 250 r/min.&lt;SEP&gt;Stirring Speed is a controlled experimental parameter set at 250 r/min to influence the leaching process dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791039701</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Liquid-Solid Ratio">
  <data key="d0">Liquid-Solid Ratio</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Liquid-Solid Ratio is a controlled experimental parameter set at 4:1 to optimize the leaching conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791039701</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Jialin Qing">
  <data key="d0">Jialin Qing</data>
