  <data key="d5">1791208777</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Table 3">
  <data key="d0">Table 3</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">Table 3 is a generic data presentation label that appears across multiple independent scientific studies, with its specific content and purpose varying significantly depending on the research context. In the field of mineral processing and phosphogypsum (PG) utilization, Table 3 documents the mass fractions of major elements in phosphogypsum samples collected from various phosphate fertilizer factories. It also summarizes the operating conditions and extraction efficiencies associated with the leaching of rare earth elements from these phosphogypsum materials.

In materials science and construction research, Table 3 presents data related to composite cement formulations and sodium chloride treatments. This version of the table lists the average grain size values for different composite cement samples. It further details the mechanical property data for these composites, alongside comprehensive measurements of water absorption, microstructural characteristics, and mechanical performance across varying concentrations of sodium chloride.

In agricultural and botanical studies, Table 3 serves as a reference for physiological measurements in plant samples. Specifically, it documents the chlorophyll and vitamin C content across various plant specimens subjected to different experimental treatments. This data table is frequently referenced in related scientific texts to support analyses of plant nutritional status and the efficacy of applied treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 3 is a data table presenting the content of selected rare earth elements in dihydrate phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Table 3 provides literature values for terrestrial materials used for comparison with phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189431</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
