<node id="Radium">
  <data key="d0">Radium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Radium is a radioactive element present in phosphogypsum that poses risks of permeation into water bodies.&lt;SEP&gt;An element with an ionic radius too large for apatite, likely co-precipitated with Barium or Strontium in phosphorite.&lt;SEP&gt;A radioactive element whose leachability from phosphogypsum was evaluated, with estimates indicating 89% remains in the crystal structure.&lt;SEP&gt;A radioactive element whose release from phosphate rock and uranium mine wastes is documented in multiple reports.&lt;SEP&gt;A radioactive element associated with uranium and thorium in phosphate materials and phosphogypsum stockpiles.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium is a radioactive element found in phosphogypsum, requiring careful monitoring and removal processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium is a radioactive element identified in phosphogypsum leachates and soil systems.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-401b567da916dc34559e0bfe5a5b367b-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-040&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-036&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-043&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023</data>
