<node id="SBF Solution">
  <data key="d0">SBF Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">A simulated body fluid in which composite bone cements were immersed to evaluate in vitro apatite formation.&lt;SEP&gt;SBF Solution is a simulated body fluid solution used to evaluate the apatite-forming ability of bone cements.&lt;SEP&gt;SBF Solution is a simulated body fluid with ion concentration matching human blood plasma, used for in vitro screening of bone bioactive materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A simulated body fluid used to immerse bone cement samples to evaluate apatite precipitation and bioactivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Simulated Body Fluid used to evaluate the in vitro apatite-forming ability and biocompatibility of the material.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791060335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In Vitro Apatite Formation">
  <data key="d0">In Vitro Apatite Formation</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">A biological evaluation process conducted by immersing bone cements in SBF solution to assess bioactivity.&lt;SEP&gt;In Vitro Apatite Formation is an experimental procedure where composite bone cements are immersed in SBF to confirm apatite formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791060335</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="In Vitro Cytotoxicity Test">
  <data key="d0">In Vitro Cytotoxicity Test</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">In Vitro Cytotoxicity Test is a screening procedure performed to evaluate the cytotoxicity of the prepared materials.&lt;SEP&gt;A laboratory procedure used to evaluate the toxicity of materials on specific cell types over a 12 to 24 hour period.&lt;SEP&gt;In Vitro Cytotoxicity Test is a laboratory procedure used to evaluate the biocompatibility and cell safety of the composite bone cement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016</data>
