<node id="Cell Viability">
  <data key="d0">Cell Viability</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Cell Viability is a quantitative metric showing above 94.12% survival rate for cells exposed to the composite cement.&lt;SEP&gt;A quantitative metric measuring the percentage of living cells after material exposure, used to assess biocompatibility.&lt;SEP&gt;Cell viability is a quantitative metric measured in percentages to assess the health and survival of cells under experimental conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791060605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bone Ingrowth">
  <data key="d0">Bone Ingrowth</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The biological process of new bone tissue growing into a material, which is enhanced by higher porosity and pore size.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791060605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Composite Bone Cement">
  <data key="d0">Composite Bone Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Composite Bone Cement is a synthetic biomaterial engineered specifically for medical and bone tissue-engineering applications, with a primary focus on bone repair. It is formulated from calcium sulfate and hydroxyapatite in a 0.70CaS–0.30HAP ratio, with sodium chloride incorporated at varying concentrations to tailor its performance. Throughout experimental procedures, this material serves as the central engineered substance under investigation.

Researchers have extensively evaluated its physical, microstructural, and mechanical properties, alongside its phase composition, washout resistance, and setting time. The deliberate modification of sodium chloride levels directly influences these characteristics, prompting detailed analyses of fracture surfaces to assess porosity levels. Furthermore, the cement's surface properties and apatite formation capability are closely examined to determine its bioactivity. In addition to structural and mechanical assessments, the material undergoes rigorous biological testing, including cytotoxicity and biocompatibility evaluations, to ensure its safety and efficacy for bone-related and broader biomedical applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791060605</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Specific Surface Area">
  <data key="d0">Specific Surface Area</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">A physical property of porous structures that influences loading rates, active site availability, and overall biocompatibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791060605</data>
