<node id="Porosity">
  <data key="d0">Porosity</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Porosity is a fundamental physical and structural property that quantifies the percentage or volume fraction of void space within a material. In the context of cement and composite bone cements, porosity represents the proportion of empty spaces within the hardened structure. This characteristic is directly influenced by the addition of sodium chloride; as sodium chloride concentration or additive content increases, the porosity of the cement matrix correspondingly rises. This elevated porosity significantly alters the material's physical and mechanical profile by reducing overall density and exerting an inverse, exponential effect on bending strength. Furthermore, the increased void structure created by higher sodium chloride levels is functionally beneficial in biomedical applications, as it facilitates and promotes the precipitation of apatite crystals, which is crucial for bone integration.

In soil science, porosity is similarly defined as a physical property measured as a percentage, representing the ratio of void volume to total soil volume. Its value is highly dynamic and responds to agricultural and chemical amendments. Specifically, porosity in soil has been observed to increase significantly following the application of biofertilizers. This enhancement in soil porosity is primarily driven by calcium-induced flocculation processes, which reorganize soil particles into more stable aggregates. Consequently, these structural improvements lead to a more open soil matrix with greater void space, thereby enhancing overall soil structure and aeration.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-030</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189571</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
