<node id="Reference Intensity Ratio Method">
  <data key="d0">Reference Intensity Ratio Method</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference Intensity Ratio Method is the calculation technique used to determine the quantitative phase composition from diffraction data.&lt;SEP&gt;A quantitative analytical procedure used to calculate the precise percentage composition of each crystalline phase.&lt;SEP&gt;The Reference Intensity Ratio method is a technique used to analyze the phase composition of composite bone cements.&lt;SEP&gt;A quantitative analysis method used to calculate phase composition percentages from X-ray diffraction data.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-003</data>
