<node id="Brushite">
  <data key="d0">Brushite</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Brushite is a mixed phase identified in the composite bone cement samples via X-ray pattern.&lt;SEP&gt;Dicalcium phosphate dihydrate, identified as a secondary crystalline phase in the cement composition.&lt;SEP&gt;Brushite is a by-product phase formed in the cement system from calcium and hydrogen phosphate ions.&lt;SEP&gt;Brushite is a calcium phosphate mineral phase found in the XRD pattern of the composite bone cement.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061042</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcium Sulfate Cement">
  <data key="d0">Calcium Sulfate Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcium sulfate cement is a material that undergoes a multi-step chemical setting reaction to harden.&lt;SEP&gt;A bone cement material investigated for its physicochemical properties and use in bone repair.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-019</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bone Cement">
  <data key="d0">Bone Cement</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">The composite material subjected to density, porosity, microstructural, and mechanical property testing in the study.&lt;SEP&gt;Bone cement is a hardened material formed through crystal interlocking, noted for high binding properties and biological compatibility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-004</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Setting Reaction">
  <data key="d0">Setting Reaction</data>
  <data key="d1">event</data>
  <data key="d2">The setting reaction is a multi-step chemical process involving dissolution, saturation, precipitation, and crystal growth.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Biological Compatibility">
  <data key="d0">Biological Compatibility</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Biological compatibility is a property enhanced by gypsum and brushite cements, improving interaction with living tissues.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Hydrogen Phosphate Ion">
  <data key="d0">Hydrogen Phosphate Ion</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrogen phosphate ion is a chemical species that contributes to the formation of brushite as a by-product.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Secondary Nucleation">
  <data key="d0">Secondary Nucleation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Secondary nucleation is a crystal growth mechanism where nuclei develop into larger crystals during cement hardening.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Supersaturation">
  <data key="d0">Supersaturation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Supersaturation is a chemical condition achieved in the solution that triggers the precipitation of calcium sulfate dihydrate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061208</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Aqua Solution">
  <data key="d0">Aqua Solution</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Aqua solution is the aqueous medium surrounding cement particles where ion saturation and dissolution occur.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-b8bd3776c87a0bcab21842e8e2bb2e06-chunk-008</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791061208</data>
