  <data key="d2">Carbon monoxide is a syngas component influenced by the PG/lignite molar ratio, temperature, and water vapor in descending order.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon monoxide is a primary gaseous product generated through the reaction of calcium sulfate with carbon and the reaction of carbon with carbon dioxide.</data>
