<node id="Natural Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">Natural Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Natural Gypsum is a mineral resource historically used as a raw material for sulfuric acid and cement co-production.&lt;SEP&gt;A natural mineral with physical properties similar to phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural gypsum is a traditional raw material that is being substituted by phosphogypsum in cement retarder applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural gypsum serves as the baseline material for constructing conventional production models of cement retarders and β-building gypsum powder.&lt;SEP&gt;Natural Gypsum is a raw material whose extraction and crushing processes are avoided by recycling technologies, thereby reducing fossil resource consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;A material compared against PCR technology, which emits less particulate matter.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006</data>
