<node id="Surface Water">
  <data key="d0">Surface Water</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Surface water is a surface aquatic environment impacted by the runoff of contaminated water from phosphogypsum sites.&lt;SEP&gt;Surface water, such as lakes, receives migrating heavy metal complexes via surface runoff.&lt;SEP&gt;The Surface Water is an environmental compartment receiving direct erosion from the stack and soil erosion, acting as a water source.</data>
