<node id="Mercury">
  <data key="d0">Mercury</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Mercury is a heavy metal with the strictest regulatory limits among those listed in the water quality standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Mercury is a trace element depleted in phosphorites relative to shale.&lt;SEP&gt;Mercury is a trace element reported at very high levels in Tunisian phosphogypsum and highly contaminating according to Quebec standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Mercury is a heavy metal contaminant detected at elevated levels in groundwater near phosphogypsum stacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Mercury is a chemical element explicitly noted with units of µg l⁻¹ in the data analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element with a limit of 0.002 mg l⁻¹ and a WHO guideline value of 0.001 mg l⁻¹.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-046&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047</data>
