  <data key="d2">A major element present in phosphogypsum samples, with measured mass fractions ranging from 0.010% to 0.080%.&lt;SEP&gt;Manganese is a trace element depleted in phosphorites relative to crustal abundances.&lt;SEP&gt;Manganese is a chemical element listed in the water quality standards table with specified concentration limits.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element with a limit of 0.05 mg l⁻¹ and a WHO guideline value of 50 mg l⁻¹.</data>
