<node id="Composting Process">
  <data key="d0">Composting Process</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">The Composting Process is the experimental procedure during which microbial population changes and soil treatments were monitored.&lt;SEP&gt;Composting Process is a biological decomposition cycle characterized by distinct temperature phases and microbial activity.&lt;SEP&gt;A biological decomposition procedure where temperature and moisture are controlled to promote microbial growth and fermentation.&lt;SEP&gt;Biological decomposition method where temperature and microbial reproduction are closely linked.&lt;SEP&gt;The composting process involves microbial activity that alters the physicochemical properties of the waste mixture.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-006</data>
