<node id="Biofertilizer">
  <data key="d0">Biofertilizer</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Biofertilizer is an environmentally friendly soil amendment and microbial-enhanced fertilizer designed to improve agricultural productivity and soil health. It is typically produced through composting or microbial fermentation by combining waste resources such as straw, phosphogypsum, and livestock or chicken manure, often supplemented with composite microbial agents. The primary function of Biofertilizer is to increase soil nutrient content, enhance its physical properties, and boost overall soil fertility. When applied to soil or plants at varying ratios, it effectively promotes plant growth and improves the nutritional quality of crops.

In scientific research and experimental settings, Biofertilizer is frequently utilized as a treatment variable, where its effects are systematically evaluated and compared against untreated soil to assess its impact on plant development and soil conditions. This experimental application highlights its role as a controlled substance for studying agricultural enhancements and validating its efficacy in real-world farming scenarios.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791141041</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chloroflexi">
  <data key="d0">Chloroflexi</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">A bacterial phylum making up 2.72% of the microbial community during composting.&lt;SEP&gt;Chloroflexi is a bacterial phylum represented in the Circos plot with a corresponding color code and abundance scale.&lt;SEP&gt;A bacterial taxonomic group represented by green ribbons in the Circos plot, showing visible connections in Group A1 samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Chloroflexi is a bacterial phylum that is more abundant in Group A2_1.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-017</data>
