<node id="Straw">
  <data key="d0">Straw</data>
  <data key="d1">other</data>
  <data key="d2">Straw is a waste biomass material combined with phosphogypsum to prepare the biofertilizer.&lt;SEP&gt;Straw is a primary feedstock component used in the composting mixture.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic material added to soil to improve physical structure and porosity.&lt;SEP&gt;Straw is agricultural residue added to soil to improve porosity, structure, and water infiltration rate.&lt;SEP&gt;Straw is an agricultural waste material combined with phosphogypsum and chicken manure for biofertilizer production.&lt;SEP&gt;Agricultural residue used as a mulching amendment to prevent aggregate disintegration and control runoff.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-031</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chicken Manure">
  <data key="d0">Chicken Manure</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Chicken manure serves as a primary nitrogen source in composting mixtures to support microbial activity and soil fertility.&lt;SEP&gt;Chicken manure is a primary feedstock component used in the composting mixture.&lt;SEP&gt;Chicken manure is an organic material combined with phosphogypsum and straw for biofertilizer production.&lt;SEP&gt;Chicken manure is an organic waste material used alongside phosphogypsum and straw in the biofertilizer formulation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791141567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Microbial Fermentation Technology">
  <data key="d0">Microbial Fermentation Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Microbial fermentation technology is utilized to prepare biofertilizers by treating organic materials like straw and phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Microbial fermentation technology is the process used to convert waste resources into biofertilizers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-001</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791141567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Actinomycetes">
  <data key="d0">Actinomycetes</data>
  <data key="d1">creature</data>
  <data key="d2">Actinomycetes are microorganisms that dominate the compost community due to their metabolic roles.&lt;SEP&gt;Actinomycetes are a group of bacteria whose community structure is controlled by land use intensity.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
