</node>
<node id="Plant Biomass">
  <data key="d0">Plant Biomass</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Plant biomass is a growth metric significantly enhanced by the application of phosphogypsum biofertilizer.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791141567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Chlorophyll">
  <data key="d0">Chlorophyll</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Chlorophyll is a pigment content measured in ryegrass and pakchoi using UV spectrophotometry.&lt;SEP&gt;Chlorophyll is a pigment measured in the plants to assess physiological changes due to fertilization.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant compound whose content was tested to highlight growth in the fertilization group.&lt;SEP&gt;Chlorophyll levels in plant leaves are increased by the application of phosphogypsum biofertilizer.&lt;SEP&gt;Chlorophyll is a plant pigment whose content was estimated using aerial imaging technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Chlorophyll is a pigment extracted and analyzed from Canna Edulis Ker using specific identification and extraction processes.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791141567</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Vitamin C">
  <data key="d0">Vitamin C</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Vitamin C is a nutrient content measured in ryegrass and pakchoi to determine plant nutritional value.&lt;SEP&gt;Vitamin C is a compound whose concentration is quantified using a calibration plot established through spectrophotometric measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Vitamin C is a nutrient measured in the plants to evaluate nutritional quality under different fertilizer treatments.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant compound whose content was tested to highlight growth in the fertilization group.&lt;SEP&gt;Vitamin C concentrations in plant leaves are elevated following biofertilizer application.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-e290dd6268316238694f70c30a367426-chunk-006</data>
