<node id="Gamma Radiation">
  <data key="d0">Gamma Radiation</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Gamma radiation is a direct exposure risk associated with phosphogypsum storage.&lt;SEP&gt;Gamma Radiation is a form of aerial radioactive exposure originating from phosphogypsum stacks.&lt;SEP&gt;A type of radiation with a small quality factor where the absorbed dose typically equals the equivalent dose in man.&lt;SEP&gt;Radiation emitted directly from phosphogypsum stacks due to Radium-226 and its decay products.&lt;SEP&gt;Gamma radiation is emitted from phosphogypsum stacks and measured to assess radiological exposure levels relative to public dose limits.&lt;SEP&gt;Gamma Radiation is emitted from the Gypsum Stack and exposes humans and animals.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-025&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045</data>
