<node id="U.S. Environmental Protection Agency">
  <data key="d0">U.S. Environmental Protection Agency</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency regulates phosphogypsum use in agriculture by setting maximum Radium-226 concentration limits.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency published a comprehensive report on radionuclide interactions with soil and rock media.&lt;SEP&gt;U.S. Environmental Protection Agency is a federal agency that published reports on radioactivity distribution in phosphate industry by-products.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency published reports on techniques for reducing fluoride emissions from gypsum ponds.&lt;SEP&gt;A U.S. federal agency that published a report on the effects of the phosphate industry on radium-226 in groundwater.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency issued environmental impact statements and emission standards for radionuclides.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. Environmental Protection Agency published the user's guide for the Industrial Source Complex dispersion model.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-037&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-039&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-044&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032</data>
