<node id="Central Florida">
  <data key="d0">Central Florida</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">Central Florida is a geographic region used as a baseline for comparing trace element levels in South African phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Central Florida is a sub-region of Florida referenced for Ra-226 measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Central Florida is the geographic region where AMAX Phosphate Inc. and USS Agri-Chemicals Plant are located.&lt;SEP&gt;Central Florida is a region containing operational stacks on limestone bedrock with phosphatic clay deposits.&lt;SEP&gt;Central Florida is a region where Roessler and Guidry conducted analyses of radiological hazards and emissions from phosphogypsum stacks.&lt;SEP&gt;Central Florida is a region noted for phosphogypsum storage facilities and associated environmental hazard assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;Central Florida is a geographic region containing phosphate industry waste disposal sites studied for water quality and hydrogeology.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-035&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-041</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
