  <data key="d0">May</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">May is a researcher who provided phosphogypsum data from Florida.&lt;SEP&gt;May is a researcher who evaporated phosphogypsum leachate and used X-ray diffraction to analyze trace element compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;A researcher who evaluated the leachability of radium and toxic elements in phosphogypsum using E.P.A. procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;May conducted laboratory and field studies on the leaching characteristics and toxicity of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;May conducted studies measuring increases in soil Radium-226 concentration following phosphogypsum applications.</data>
