<node id="Phosphogypsum Stacks">
  <data key="d0">Phosphogypsum Stacks</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Storage sites for phosphogypsum that pose environmental risks such as atmospheric contamination and groundwater pollution.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum stacks are industrial structures where phosphogypsum is deposited using acidic process water.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial structures investigated for radon exhalation rates and radioactive exposure levels.&lt;SEP&gt;Man-made piles of industrial waste that emit radon-222 and gamma radiation, with exposure levels varying based on covering and moisture.&lt;SEP&gt;Storage sites for phosphogypsum that are sources of Radon-222 exhalation and potential occupational hazards.&lt;SEP&gt;Industrial structures in central Florida that were monitored for radon and airborne particulates.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-038&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791185732</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="U.S. E.P.A.">
  <data key="d0">U.S. E.P.A.</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">A regulatory body that issued a final ruling requiring phosphogypsum to be placed in stacks or mines.&lt;SEP&gt;A regulatory agency that adopted exposure limits based on risk assessments of phosphogypsum stacks.&lt;SEP&gt;The regulatory agency that adopted a limit on Rn-222 emissions from phosphogypsum stacks based on risk assessments.&lt;SEP&gt;The U.S. E.P.A. is a regulatory agency that established concentration limits for Ra-226 in phosphogypsum intended for agricultural use.&lt;SEP&gt;The regulatory body that adopted an upper limit on Radon-222 emissions from phosphogypsum stacks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-034&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-033</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791185905</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Federal Register">
  <data key="d0">Federal Register</data>
  <data key="d1">content</data>
  <data key="d2">The Federal Register published the E.P.A. allowable toxic elemental criteria for hazardous waste classification.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Register published the 1990 final ruling by the U.S. E.P.A. regarding phosphogypsum storage.&lt;SEP&gt;The official publication where the U.S. E.P.A. limit on Rn-222 emissions was documented in 1989.&lt;SEP&gt;The Federal Register published the U.S. Environmental Protection Agency ruling regarding phosphogypsum use in agriculture.&lt;SEP&gt;Federal Register is the official journal of the U.S. federal government where the E.P.A. ruling on phosphogypsum was published.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-033</data>
