<node id="Shale">
  <data key="d0">Shale</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Shale is a common marine and surficial rock used as the primary baseline for comparing trace element enrichment and depletion in phosphorites.&lt;SEP&gt;Shale is a terrestrial reference material used to compare the elemental composition of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Shale is a terrestrial material included in the table for comparative trace element analysis.&lt;SEP&gt;Shale is a sedimentary rock type used as a terrestrial reference material for chemical concentration comparison.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005</data>
