<node id="Selenium">
  <data key="d0">Selenium</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Selenium is a trace element enriched in phosphorites, frequently associated with organic matter.&lt;SEP&gt;Selenium is a trace element that, like arsenic, did not decrease greatly with pH increases and poses an environmental risk.&lt;SEP&gt;Selenium is a chemical element studied in the context of heavy metals in soils.&lt;SEP&gt;A chemical element with a specified limit of 0.01 mg l⁻¹ across multiple regulatory frameworks.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-041&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-047</data>
