  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Radium-228">
  <data key="d0">Radium-228</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Radium-228 is a radium isotope present at very low concentrations as a product of the Th-232 decay series.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-228 is a radionuclide mentioned in the context of phosphogypsum radioactivity sources.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-228 is the second most abundant radium isotope, formed in the Th-232 decay series, but rare in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-228 is a radioactive isotope of radium monitored in drinking water for radiological safety.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-003</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Th-230">
  <data key="d0">Th-230</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Th-230 is a radioactive isotope measured in Florida with a recorded value of 113.&lt;SEP&gt;Th-230 is a decay product in the U-238 series that undergoes alpha decay to form Radium-226.&lt;SEP&gt;Thorium-230 is a radioactive isotope that undergoes alpha decay to form Radium-226 within the U-238 decay series.&lt;SEP&gt;Th-230 is a radioactive isotope measured at AMAX, USSAC, Plant A, Plant B, and Plant C.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-012&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Radium Sulfate">
  <data key="d0">Radium Sulfate</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Radium Sulfate is a highly insoluble compound that precipitates early during phosphoric acid production and co-precipitates with Barium Sulfate.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-013</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
