<node id="Emanation Coefficient">
  <data key="d0">Emanation Coefficient</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The emanation coefficient quantifies the fraction of Radon-222 atoms that escape from solid crystal structures during radioactive decay.&lt;SEP&gt;A measured parameter representing the fraction of Rn-222 atoms escaping the solid phase relative to those formed.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-016</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Anaerobic Conditions">
  <data key="d0">Anaerobic Conditions</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Anaerobic conditions promote bacterially mediated redox reactions that indirectly solubilize heavy metals and radionuclides like Ra-226.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-015</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791188710</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
