<node id="USSAC">
  <data key="d0">USSAC</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">USSAC is an organization associated with the source of phosphogypsum process water data reported by Miller and Sutcliffe Jr.&lt;SEP&gt;USSAC is a reference dataset or standard used to report geochemical concentration values.&lt;SEP&gt;USSAC is an industrial facility where radioactive isotopes and process waters were sampled.&lt;SEP&gt;USSAC is an industrial site where radionuclide activities in phosphogypsum process water were measured.&lt;SEP&gt;USSAC is a site or entity referenced as a sampling location in the Miller and Sutcliffe Jr. (1982) study.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-021&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-020&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-045&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-019&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-022</data>
