  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Acid soils are subsoils in tropical and subtropical areas characterized by phytotoxic aluminum levels and deficient calcium that restrict root exploitation.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Calcareous Soils">
  <data key="d0">Calcareous Soils</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Calcareous soils are a soil type where phosphogypsum application increases the availability of nitrogen, phosphorus, potassium, and magnesium.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phytophthora Infection">
  <data key="d0">Phytophthora Infection</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phytophthora infection is a disease affecting citrus roots that can be reduced by phosphogypsum application.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Peanut Pod Rot">
  <data key="d0">Peanut Pod Rot</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Peanut pod rot is a disease linked to excess magnesium and potassium displaced from the soil exchange complex by calcium from phosphogypsum.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Phytotoxic Aluminum">
  <data key="d0">Phytotoxic Aluminum</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Phytotoxic aluminum is a toxic form of aluminum in acid soils that inhibits root growth by disrupting cell division during mitosis.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Root Proliferation">
  <data key="d0">Root Proliferation</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Root proliferation is the enhanced root growth observed in soils where phosphogypsum application reduced phytotoxic aluminum levels.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Dissolution Rate">
  <data key="d0">Dissolution Rate</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Dissolution rate is the speed at which phosphogypsum breaks down, partially controlling its effectiveness as a soil amendment.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-029</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Mordvedt">
  <data key="d0">Mordvedt</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">Mordvedt conducted studies measuring increases in soil Radium-226 concentration following phosphogypsum applications.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="McDowell-Boyer">
  <data key="d0">McDowell-Boyer</data>
  <data key="d1">person</data>
  <data key="d2">McDowell-Boyer provided typical Radium-226 concentration values for U.S. grain products.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="National Council of Radiation Protection">
  <data key="d0">National Council of Radiation Protection</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The National Council of Radiation Protection establishes guidelines for Radium-226 limits in soil used for growing food crops.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Federal Radiation Council">
  <data key="d0">Federal Radiation Council</data>
  <data key="d1">organization</data>
  <data key="d2">The Federal Radiation Council provides guidance on dietary uptake levels that the studied intake exceeds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Bone Surface Dose">
  <data key="d0">Bone Surface Dose</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Bone Surface Dose is a measured radiation metric calculated for individuals consuming grain from phosphogypsum-treated land.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Committed Effective Dose Equivalent">
  <data key="d0">Committed Effective Dose Equivalent</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Committed Effective Dose Equivalent is a radiation metric representing 20% of the National Council of Radiation Protection recommendation for public exposure.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Residential Occupancy">
  <data key="d0">Residential Occupancy</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Residential Occupancy refers to living conditions whose safety guidelines are exceeded by radon daughter concentrations from contaminated soil.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Grain Products">
  <data key="d0">Grain Products</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Grain Products are food items consumed by humans that may contain Radium-226 originating from phosphogypsum-treated land.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-032</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791189785</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Uranium Tailings">
  <data key="d0">Uranium Tailings</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Uranium tailings are referenced as a source of soil contamination relevant to federal concentration limits for residential construction.</data>
