<node id="Alkali Neutralization Treatment">
  <data key="d0">Alkali Neutralization Treatment</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">Alkali neutralization treatment is a modification process applied to phosphogypsum to reduce harmful impurities.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791207188</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="β-Building Gypsum">
  <data key="d0">β-Building Gypsum</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">β-Building gypsum is a construction material powder produced from processed phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;β-Building Gypsum is a building product utilizing phosphogypsum with sales radii generally limited to within 100 kilometers.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791207316</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Quicklime">
  <data key="d0">Quicklime</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Quicklime, a chemical compound chemically equivalent to calcium oxide, serves as a fundamental raw material and resource input across several industrial process scenarios, notably PCR and PBG. It functions primarily as a neutralizing and modifying agent within alkali neutralization treatments. In this capacity, quicklime is specifically deployed to react with and neutralize harmful acids and acidic impurities present in phosphogypsum.

The utilization of quicklime in these processes requires high-temperature calcination, a treatment step that inherently releases carbon dioxide emissions. Due to its substantial consumption and the energy demands of its processing, quicklime constitutes a major factor in the ecological footprint of these operations. It is responsible for up to 99.9% of the various environmental burdens associated with the PCR and PBG scenarios, highlighting its significant environmental impact alongside its industrial utility.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-015&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-014&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-016&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791207316</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Coal-Fired Hot Air Furnaces">
  <data key="d0">Coal-Fired Hot Air Furnaces</data>
  <data key="d1">artifact</data>
  <data key="d2">Coal-fired hot air furnaces provide the heat sources for the drying and calcination stages in β-building gypsum production.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-002</data>
