<node id="PBG Technology">
  <data key="d0">PBG Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PBG technology is one of three representative PG resource-utilization technologies analyzed in the life cycle inventory.&lt;SEP&gt;PBG Technology is a Plaster of Paris utilization method that demonstrates minor impacts on fossil resource depletion due to product substitution effects.&lt;SEP&gt;A phosphogypsum disposal technology negatively impacted mainly by coal and electricity consumption.&lt;SEP&gt;PBG Technology is a phosphogypsum utilization method that recovers β-building gypsum powder and achieves the highest net economic profit.&lt;SEP&gt;PBG Technology is a phosphogypsum utilization method that yields the lowest net profit among the compared technologies.&lt;SEP&gt;PBG technology is a PG resource utilization pathway that yields the highest net economic gain among the studied methods.&lt;SEP&gt;PBG Technology is a Phosphogypsum resource utilization method that generates the largest share of economic revenue.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791208013</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Net Profit">
  <data key="d0">Net Profit</data>
  <data key="d1">data</data>
  <data key="d2">Net Profit is an economic metric measuring the financial gain generated by different resource utilization technologies.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791208267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PCR Technology">
  <data key="d0">PCR Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PCR Technology is a phosphogypsum resource utilization method, occasionally referenced in relation to plaster of Paris processing, that currently represents 12.7% of the baseline utilization rate. It is classified as one of three representative phosphogypsum resource-utilization technologies evaluated within a life cycle inventory framework. Among these alternatives, PCR Technology is distinguished by its straightforward operational workflow and the lowest associated costs. The core mechanism of the process involves the application of quicklime to facilitate chemical neutralization, which dictates both its economic efficiency and its environmental trajectory.

The environmental profile of PCR Technology presents a complex trade-off between operational advantages and chemical dependencies. On one hand, the method yields significant benefits in resource and energy conservation, delivers moderate reductions in carbon emissions, and improves potential outcomes for human health and ecological toxicity. On the other hand, the heavy reliance on quicklime introduces substantial environmental burdens, making quicklime consumption the primary driver of negative ecological impacts. Consequently, while PCR Technology offers a highly accessible and cost-effective pathway for phosphogypsum management, its overall sustainability is heavily contingent upon mitigating the environmental footprint associated with quicklime production and usage.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791208267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fossil Resources">
  <data key="d0">Fossil Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Fossil Resources are natural reserves that experience increased depletion when PSC Technology proportions exceed specific thresholds.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791208267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="PSC Technology">
  <data key="d0">PSC Technology</data>
  <data key="d1">method</data>
  <data key="d2">PSC Technology is a phosphogypsum (PG) and Plaster of Paris resource utilization method that has been evaluated as one of three representative PG utilization technologies in a life cycle inventory. The production process is heavily dependent on fuel coal and coke, with calcination and drying stages accounting for the majority of coal consumption. Despite representing the highest-cost option among analyzed methods and exhibiting the highest fossil resource impact, the technology yields the lowest global warming potential and generates a diverse range of commercial products, including sulfuric acid and cement.

Environmentally, PSC Technology significantly reduces metal and water resource consumption while supporting circular utilization practices and delivering substantial ecological benefits. Although it requires substantial fossil inputs and incurs higher operational costs, its long-term environmental performance and economic advantages make it a highly viable industrial solution. Consequently, PSC Technology is consistently recommended for large-scale and widespread adoption across the phosphogypsum management sector.</data>
  <data key="d3">doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-011&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-006&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-276f29345df37143fc224a22d0f6089b-chunk-012</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1791208267</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Metal Resources">
  <data key="d0">Metal Resources</data>
  <data key="d1">naturalobject</data>
  <data key="d2">Metal Resources are natural reserves that achieve maximum conservation when PSC Technology proportions are maximized.</data>
