  <data key="d8">pH is identified as the primary factor explaining the chemical behavior and reactivity of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;pH is identified as the primary factor explaining the chemical behavior and reactivity of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum dumping reduces seawater and soil pH, creating highly acidic conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;pH is identified as the primary factor explaining the chemical behavior and reactivity of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;pH is a key property measured to characterize the acidity of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum application results in significant reductions in the pH of alkaline, saline, and saline-sodic soils.&lt;SEP&gt;pH is a measured chemical parameter in Phosphogypsum samples.</data>
