  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum is not pure calcium sulfate but contains various impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate is the chemical class encompassing gypsum, bassanite, and anhydrite found in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum may contain Calcium Sulfate as a measured component.&lt;SEP&gt;Calcium sulfate is a primary chemical component of phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is rich in calcium resources primarily existing as calcium sulfate.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum's main component is calcium sulfate, which enables its use as an oxygen carrier.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is primarily composed of calcium sulfate.</data>
