<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Organic Matter">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum contains organic matter that is reduced through citric acid treatment and washing.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains organic matter as a residual impurity that is targeted for removal.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic Matter is a chemical component measured within Phosphogypsum samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains organic matter as a distinct category of impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic matter accumulates near phosphogypsum sites, decreasing the soil's nutrient retention and supply capacity.&lt;SEP&gt;Organic matter is an impurity present in phosphogypsum solids.</data>
  <data key="d9">causes accumulation,chemical analysis,chemical composition,composition,contains,contains impurity,impurity classification,reduces fertility</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-007&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-005</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791190433</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Fluoride">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Fluoride and Phosphogypsum are linked by the presence of fluoride as a significant chemical component and impurity within phosphogypsum samples. Phosphogypsum consistently contains elevated concentrations of fluoride, which can be released into the surrounding environment as gas or dust during processing and storage. Additionally, water interacting with phosphogypsum frequently generates leachate containing fluoride levels that exceed established drinking water safety standards.

Once introduced into the ecosystem, fluoride from phosphogypsum can be adsorbed into topsoil or absorbed by vegetation. Due to its classification as a primary pollutant responsible for causing fluorosis, the presence of fluoride in phosphogypsum represents a major environmental concern. This contamination risk significantly restricts the material's potential for agricultural application, making fluoride management a critical factor in phosphogypsum handling and disposal.</data>
  <data key="d9">chemical analysis,composition,contains,contamination,environmental concern,impurity,leachate composition,toxicity,trace element source</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-001fe856b0d193d82422dc8a5baedc86-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-005&lt;SEP&gt;doc-34a3ac199714be8fd1cdff8ead90fc92-chunk-009&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-018&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-028&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-023&lt;SEP&gt;doc-fbe0ad1b5f7f65c2338dc42cd9ca4b89-chunk-033</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791190060</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Phosphate Fertilizer Production">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphate Fertilizer Production generates Phosphogypsum as a chemical byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate fertilizer production generates phosphogypsum as a major byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate fertilizer production generates phosphogypsum as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is generated as a byproduct of phosphate fertilizer production.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphate fertilizer production generates phosphogypsum as a byproduct.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is generated as a byproduct of phosphate fertilizer production.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is generated as a byproduct of phosphate fertilizer production.</data>
