<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Fluorides">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum contains fluorides that must be removed to meet safety and quality standards.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorides are impurities in phosphogypsum derived from rock phosphate, present as various sodium and calcium compounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains fluorides as primary potentially toxic elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Fluorides are impurities present in phosphogypsum solids.</data>
