<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Radium-226">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Radium-226 is a radioactive component found in phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is enriched with Radium-226 and other radionuclides from its production process.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 content in phosphogypsum exceeds levels found in fly ash and soil.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 is a major source of radioactivity in phosphogypsum, formed by the alpha decay of Th-230.&lt;SEP&gt;Radium-226 is a primary source of radioactivity found within Phosphogypsum.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Radium-226, which is measured in soil and crops following application.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains Radium-226, which contributes to soil radioactivity upon application.</data>
  <data key="d9">component of,concentration comparison,contains,decay product,enrichment,geochemical distribution,major component,radioactive component,radioactive source,radioactivity source</data>
