<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Wet Process">
  <data key="d7">5.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The wet process generates phosphogypsum as a major solid byproduct alongside phosphoric acid.&lt;SEP&gt;The wet process involves chemical reactions that generate acids affecting phosphogypsum impurities.&lt;SEP&gt;The wet process generates phosphogypsum as a major byproduct during the production of phosphate fertilizers.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum is a byproduct generated through the wet process of phosphate rock treatment.&lt;SEP&gt;The type of wet process used determines the major elemental composition of phosphogypsum.</data>
