<edge source="Phosphogypsum" target="Potentially Toxic Elements">
  <data key="d7">6.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Phosphogypsum contains Potentially Toxic Elements that require careful retention and long-term management.&lt;SEP&gt;The concentration and speciation of potentially toxic elements are critical factors in assessing phosphogypsum toxicity and potential hazard.&lt;SEP&gt;Phosphogypsum contains primary potentially toxic elements such as fluorides and phosphates.&lt;SEP&gt;Potentially toxic elements accumulate and transport from phosphogypsum to stockpile sites, spreading over large spatial regions.&lt;SEP&gt;Potentially toxic elements are hazardous impurities present in phosphogypsum that limit its commercial use.&lt;SEP&gt;Potentially toxic elements are contained within phosphogypsum and pose a leaching risk to groundwater systems if not immobilized.</data>
  <data key="d9">accumulation,composition,containment,contamination,environmental hazard,hazard determination,impurity,leaching risk,safety concern,toxicity assessment</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-003&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-004&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-d1ffdf413ee3cbdda92474adf77e2c78-chunk-007</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791023386</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
