<edge source="Chemical Looping Gasification" target="Lignite">
  <data key="d7">8.0</data>
  <data key="d8">The Chemical Looping Gasification and lignite relation describes a thermochemical conversion process in which lignite functions as the primary feedstock and fuel source. This technology specifically processes lignite to generate syngas, leveraging the chemical looping mechanism to facilitate efficient gasification. The relationship centers on the integration of lignite into CLG systems, where the fuel undergoes controlled oxidation and reduction cycles to maximize carbon conversion while maintaining process stability.

Lignite, recognized as a specific low-rank coal, is extensively studied within this context for its distinct fluidization characteristics and reaction kinetics during gasification. Operational and experimental configurations of this process often employ lignite in conjunction with specialized carrier materials, such as phosphogypsum, to enhance oxygen transfer and overall reaction efficiency. Consequently, this relation highlights a targeted application of advanced gasification technology tailored to the physicochemical properties of lignite for optimized syngas production.</data>
  <data key="d9">co-processing,feedstock,fuel source,gasification,processing,processing target,substrate</data>
  <data key="d10">doc-a7ec54d376b079eceb4eab9d1f23165e-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2eed3e4bb65f425c7011f91fbc1c7dd5-chunk-010&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-027&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-026&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-024&lt;SEP&gt;doc-a3152ce135edc56e14c47e05535e05c7-chunk-008&lt;SEP&gt;doc-20b5888df3bfef8e98cc13abb005b7f0-chunk-010</data>
  <data key="d11">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d12">1791120960</data>
  <data key="d13"></data>
</edge>
<edge source="Chemical Looping Gasification" target="Syngas">
  <data key="d7">7.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Chemical looping gasification converts lignite into syngas using phosphogypsum as an oxygen carrier.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical looping gasification converts lignite into syngas using phosphogypsum as an oxygen carrier.&lt;SEP&gt;The chemical looping gasification process yields syngas as its primary product.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chemical Looping Gasification process converts lignite into syngas through non-homogeneous reactions.&lt;SEP&gt;The CLG process utilizes oxygen carriers to produce syngas from lignite.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical looping gasification produces syngas.&lt;SEP&gt;Chemical looping gasification converts lignite into syngas using phosphogypsum as an oxygen carrier.</data>
