<edge source="Uranium-238" target="Radium-226">
  <data key="d7">4.0</data>
  <data key="d8">Uranium-238 is the parent nuclide of Radium-226, with an activity ratio less than unity in the waste samples.&lt;SEP&gt;Uranium-238 acts as the parent isotope to Radium-226 in the radioactive decay chain.&lt;SEP&gt;Uranium-238 and Radium-226 activities are in approximate secular equilibrium in Florida phosphate ore.&lt;SEP&gt;Uranium-238 activity in phosphogypsum can equal that of Radium-226, raising environmental concerns.</data>
